{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic","id":1306125,"title":"The Aura mechanic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-19T18:00:18-07:00","id":1306125,"title":"The Aura mechanic","content":"So maybe it's just my extensive research on the dragon blooded charmset, but since I haven't quite played it maybe someone could just confirm it but does the aura mechanic feel bad in and out of combat? This is just from a theory point of view it looks like they aren't remotely enough charms to fairly spread out the mechanic. I was looking at other abilities to branch out to and there seems like a very small chance of actually using certain abilities together without losing a majority of your charms. There are also a lot abilities in certain trees that you can't use because of element lockout. Resistance being one that's notable. In addition, to signature charms.<br /> <br /> I think another issue I didn't think would be an issue till I saw it was the expenditure of Aura for martial arts. Because there are so many defensive aura charms dragon blooded have with not so insignificant costs, you just end up losing a lot of defensive charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:00:13-07:00","id":1306151,"title":"","content":"I'm very much not a fan of Aura. I've been running/playing a DB game for a while now and 90% of the time we just lose track of who has what Aura in between tracking motes, turns, initiative, etc. Same thing with Anima banner and Amina Flux actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:15:17-07:00","id":1306155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306151#post1306151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very much not a fan of Aura. I've been running/playing a DB game for a while now and 90% of the time we just lose track of who has what Aura in between tracking motes, turns, initiative, etc. Same thing with Anima banner and Amina Flux actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it hinder any charm use? I mean looking at it I can see trees where it happens at E3+ quite easily. Resistance seems to be unfortunate in that there are so many auras charms at different elements they are impossible to combine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:35:46-07:00","id":1306158,"title":"","content":"A lot of the low charms are balanced so it won't make you lose an aura, but there are nice charms that aren't so you'll risk entering an aura you don't want or losing one you do if you use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:37:36-07:00","id":1306159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306158#post1306158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the low charms are balanced so it won't make you lose an aura, but there are nice charms that aren't so you'll risk entering an aura you don't want or losing one you do if you use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the element. Like try using dodge with anything but fire or some air and you get utterly limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:58:12-07:00","id":1306163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306151#post1306151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very much not a fan of Aura. I've been running/playing a DB game for a while now and 90% of the time we just lose track of who has what Aura in between tracking motes, turns, initiative, etc. Same thing with Anima banner and Amina Flux actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried using a colour sided die? I'm legitimately curious because eventually I want to run Dragonblooded and I'm not sure how I want to track Aura.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306155#post1306155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it hinder any charm use? I mean looking at it I can see trees where it happens at E3+ quite easily. Resistance seems to be unfortunate in that there are so many auras charms at different elements they are impossible to combine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is kind of the point of Aura though, isn't it? To stop DBs from having the same kind of big combinational effects that Solars have, while still maintaining some powers that are solidly impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T21:26:04-07:00","id":1306167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306163#post1306163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is kind of the point of Aura though, isn't it? To stop DBs from having the same kind of big combinational effects that Solars have, while still maintaining some powers that are solidly impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without Aura a lot of those charms are sufficiently weaker. There are a few charms sorta better. Like Air athletics gets scenelong true flight even if it's completely unusable during a fight thanks to the 4i per round cost. The bigger issue is that it means a DB has a smaller charmset outside of custom charms because you have charms that lock out other charms. In addition, it also means that you are rewarded for going in a few specific ways. Since I've been looking at martial arts for the most part I'll give an example. Earth dragon + resistance or Fire dragon + dodge + presence work amazingly. However you try Wood + dodge or resistance and water + dodge and you find yourself with very few charms that work.<br /> <br /> I believe resistance has balance charms but just looking at dodge over again the only balance charm it has is the excellency. And now this wouldn't be so bad if the aura key word wasn't so important for specific effects. After a skim through a lot of the aura effects seem to be for flashy or combat effects. So that is important to note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T21:47:09-07:00","id":1306168,"title":"","content":"I haven't played Dragon-Blooded yet, but from a &quot;feels bad&quot; perspective, the thing that bugs me about Aura is that it really makes some Charms purely a &quot;Charm Tax&quot; for certain niche builds. That mostly shows up at high-Essence where you'd have a bunch of Charms anyway so you could better afford the &quot;cost,&quot; but it still doesn't feel great.<br /> <br /> Look at Mela's Flashing Tongue at Essence 4 in Melee, for instance. It's an Air Melee Charm with an Air Aura effect whose prerequisites include Crimson Fang Bite (Fire, not Balanced), Dragon Soul Burst (Fire, not Balanced), Smoldering Essence Attack (Fire, Aura-keyworded), and Burning Pinnacle Strike (Fire, Aura-keyworded). If you want the Aura effect of Mela's Flashing Tongue you have to actively avoid using <i>four other Charms</i> which you were <i>forced to learn</i> in order to learn Mela's Flashing Tongue. And while Mela's Flashing Tongue is <i>situationally</i> a <i>very</i> strong multiattack Charm, I don't know that I'd say it's the equivalent of <i>five Charms worth</i> of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T21:52:49-07:00","id":1306169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306168#post1306168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played Dragon-Blooded yet, but from a &amp;quot;feels bad&amp;quot; perspective, the thing that bugs me about Aura is that it really makes some Charms purely a &amp;quot;Charm Tax&amp;quot; for certain niche builds. That mostly shows up at high-Essence where you'd have a bunch of Charms anyway so you could better afford the &amp;quot;cost,&amp;quot; but it still doesn't feel great.<br /> <br /> Look at Mela's Flashing Tongue at Essence 4 in Melee, for instance. It's an Air Melee Charm with an Air Aura effect whose prerequisites include Crimson Fang Bite (Fire, not Balanced), Dragon Soul Burst (Fire, not Balanced), Smoldering Essence Attack (Fire, Aura-keyworded), and Burning Pinnacle Strike (Fire, Aura-keyworded). If you want the Aura effect of Mela's Flashing Tongue you have to actively avoid using <i>four other Charms</i> which you were <i>forced to learn</i> in order to learn Mela's Flashing Tongue. And while Mela's Flashing Tongue is <i>situationally</i> a <i>very</i> strong multiattack Charm, I don't know that I'd say it's the equivalent of <i>five Charms worth</i> of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s the alternative though? Not giving them the Charms that punch above their weight class? 3E\u2019s solution to those raw elemental power effects that transcend normal DB power is making a strategic limit on how they can be used. I suppose another way to do that would be to just limit them to once per scene with a reset condition, but that\u2019s also a \u201ctax\u201d under the same logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T21:53:20-07:00","id":1306170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306168#post1306168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played Dragon-Blooded yet, but from a &amp;quot;feels bad&amp;quot; perspective, the thing that bugs me about Aura is that it really makes some Charms purely a &amp;quot;Charm Tax&amp;quot; for certain niche builds. That mostly shows up at high-Essence where you'd have a bunch of Charms anyway so you could better afford the &amp;quot;cost,&amp;quot; but it still doesn't feel great.<br /> <br /> Look at Mela's Flashing Tongue at Essence 4 in Melee, for instance. It's an Air Melee Charm with an Air Aura effect whose prerequisites include Crimson Fang Bite (Fire, not Balanced), Dragon Soul Burst (Fire, not Balanced), Smoldering Essence Attack (Fire, Aura-keyworded), and Burning Pinnacle Strike (Fire, Aura-keyworded). If you want the Aura effect of Mela's Flashing Tongue you have to actively avoid using <i>four other Charms</i> which you were <i>forced to learn</i> in order to learn Mela's Flashing Tongue. And while Mela's Flashing Tongue is <i>situationally</i> a <i>very</i> strong multiattack Charm, I don't know that I'd say it's the equivalent of <i>five Charms worth</i> of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, if you are air aspected you could go into fire aura and switch to air but you'd still have to be air aspected and I don't know if you can combo it with other charms. If you have any fire aspected aura charms though you'd basically be losing them for that strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:16:48-07:00","id":1306174,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Aura empowered Mela\u2019s flashing tongue isn\u2019t situationally Good. It\u2019s situationally Amazing. The closest equivalent in the Solars set would I guess be Iron Whirlwind tech+Invincible fury of the Dawn? Only that doesn\u2019t get you any extra Initiative to spend.<br /> <br /> Like a direct comparison is tough but you\u2019re basically converting attacks from your allies into free attacks for you now. Your allies don\u2019t even have to be good at fighting, just present and vaguely aggressive (maybe attempting gambits)<br /> <br /> Like yes. It\u2019s a long way to go to get a fight-ending charm. But it will end... like Most Fights.<br /> <br /> Its primary weakness is opponents that avoid Onslaught, which is pretty much Just Exalts and even then Mostly Solars.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and like... Having Friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-20-2019, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:23:18-07:00","id":1306175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306169#post1306169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the alternative though? Not giving them the Charms that punch above their weight class? 3E\u2019s solution to those raw elemental power effects that transcend normal DB power is making a strategic limit on how they can be used. I suppose another way to do that would be to just limit them to once per scene with a reset condition, but that\u2019s also a \u201ctax\u201d under the same logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, that particular example is <i>also</i> once-per-scene with a reset condition (dealing enough damage to incapacitate a previously uninjured nontrivial enemy in a single Decisive attack).<br /> <br /> My alternative would be not adding in those high-Essence Charms in Elements that the Ability doesn't otherwise support. The big example people pointed out when the book text first came out was Arrow Rain Tempest, an Essence 5 Archery Charm that is once-per-scene with <i>no</i> reset condition, is situational in use (requires two consecutive turns aiming at 12+ Initiative before use), carries the risk of friendly fire, <i>and requires you to expend Water Aura.</i> Death From Nowhere does work to set Water Aura up using another Archery Charm (and Death From Nowhere got easier to use [if also more expensive] between the Kickstarter preview and the final text), but Water <i>really</i> doesn't have much presence in Archery, and even though Arrow Rain Tempest is genuinely very cool, it just feels to me like the support for a &quot;Water Archer&quot; play style isn't there.<br /> <br /> I suspect the Devs' argument would be that techniques like that are probably not meant to be play styles of their own... you don't take Arrow Rain Tempest because you're a &quot;Water Archer&quot; or Mela's Flashing Tongue because you're an &quot;Air Swordsman,&quot; you take them because you're a great archer or a great swordsman who will occasionally bend over backward to use This One Cool Move... but I'd rather see more elementally-limited charm sets which actually support each element they <i>do</i> include in their non-Signature Charms.<br /> <br /> (I was going to cite Brawl as an example of the kind of design I like, but I forgot that Earth Brawl doesn't have anything past Essence 3 and Wood Brawl carries a &quot;Charm Tax&quot; of a couple non-Balanced Water Charms, so I'll just say it's <i>closer</i>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:33:14-07:00","id":1306178,"title":"","content":"I disagree but I think I get where you\u2019re coming from now. It\u2019s not the direction the devs went with, and I personally like the blended charmsets, even if a charm or two are isolated. Buuut I can also see wanting a more focused build in each ability with strict elemental themes.<br /> <br /> That said, I generally don\u2019t Like activating more than like, two charms on my turn? So that\u2019s just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T23:28:01-07:00","id":1306184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306178#post1306178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree but I think I get where you\u2019re coming from now. It\u2019s not the direction the devs went with, and I personally like the blended charmsets, even if a charm or two are isolated. Buuut I can also see wanting a more focused build in each ability with strict elemental themes.<br /> <br /> That said, I generally don\u2019t Like activating more than like, two charms on my turn? So that\u2019s just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still limits you especially when you have aura charms aura charms that only last while in aura and have a willpower cost associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T00:38:32-07:00","id":1306193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306167#post1306167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe resistance has balance charms but just looking at dodge over again the only balance charm it has is the excellency. And now this wouldn't be so bad if the aura key word wasn't so important for specific effects. After a skim through a lot of the aura effects seem to be for flashy or combat effects. So that is important to note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah dodge is definitely a big one that's hard to use if you're in non-fire aura. I tend to look at it as you having 3 options most basically, although outside of test combats I haven't played much I admit.<br /> <br /> One is that you just ignore everything to do with aura, you freely match every kind of element and don't care that you never enter aura. You don't take aura charms but you take whatever else charms you want from all over the place.<br /> <br /> Another way is to just go hard into your own element and balance charms, like if you're a wood aspect who uses dodge, just take the excellency and Swaying Grass, and maybe Hopping Firecracker/Virtuous Negation Defense. Swaying Grass and the Excellency will get you to be more evasive than almost any other DB anyway, and Hopping Firecracker is there if you really need it to sacrifice your aura and get away, but if you're not using aura at the moment it's no cost anyway. For water it's much the same, just take the sig, the excellency, Heat of Battle Advance and Ebbing Tide Recedes, which can actually be used in the same action I believe, even getting the Water Aura advantage.<br /> <br /> And the third way is to try and make another element work outside of your own. Like you're a Fire aspect but you always take the Earth signature charms and be super careful about flaring your anima because it'll knock you out of the aura that you're in.<br /> <br /> Or some kind of weird advanced hybrid of all three where you use Earth charms until your anima flares, use some kind of Fire charm that expends your Aura and then fall back on mixing elements for the battle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306174#post1306174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its primary weakness is opponents that avoid Onslaught, which is pretty much Just Exalts and even then Mostly Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think it's been clarified that enemies suffering from onslaught penalties still count as having those penalties, even if they're currently ignoring them. So they might Dipping Swallow to get their defense back up, but you're still making 6 attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306175#post1306175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My alternative would be not adding in those high-Essence Charms in Elements that the Ability doesn't otherwise support. The big example people pointed out when the book text first came out was Arrow Rain Tempest, an Essence 5 Archery Charm that is once-per-scene with <i>no</i> reset condition, is situational in use (requires two consecutive turns aiming at 12+ Initiative before use), carries the risk of friendly fire, <i>and requires you to expend Water Aura.</i> Death From Nowhere does work to set Water Aura up using another Archery Charm (and Death From Nowhere got easier to use [if also more expensive] between the Kickstarter preview and the final text), but Water <i>really</i> doesn't have much presence in Archery, and even though Arrow Rain Tempest is genuinely very cool, it just feels to me like the support for a &quot;Water Archer&quot; play style isn't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This particular one at least gets waaay easier if you're a water aspect. You can enter any other aura with dodge or resistance or athletics or something, even just popping a mote with her anima power, and make sure that your last expenditure flares you totemic to automatically switch to Water Aura.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mela's Flashing Tongue is also an interesting one. What I might try to do is actually be an Air aspect, and try to fight a somewhat reserved battle in Fire Aura, before flaring totemic, switching instantly to Air Aura, and unleashing that devastating charm to finish the fight off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T01:19:53-07:00","id":1306198,"title":"","content":"You can also just make up your own charms to plug gaps if you really need to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T04:21:41-07:00","id":1306229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306193#post1306193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah dodge is definitely a big one that's hard to use if you're in non-fire aura. I tend to look at it as you having 3 options most basically, although outside of test combats I haven't played much I admit.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that basically means that a non-fire dragon dodger has a subpar build and is screwed out of effects not just within the defense tree but also the attack tree. You get more out of playing with aura flat out and end up in a situation where a fire dragon dodger or a earthdragon tank are just better than the others. Technically dragon styles can combo with other cma to fill up gaps. Like water +crane and brawls water aura effevt but native charms don't have that luxury. I also don't get how melee and dodge could even be in the same element with those kinds of issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T09:33:38-07:00","id":1306268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306229#post1306229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with that basically means that a non-fire dragon dodger has a subpar build and is screwed out of effects not just within the defense tree but also the attack tree. You get more out of playing with aura flat out and end up in a situation where a fire dragon dodger or a earthdragon tank are just better than the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually sure if that's true, in all cases anyway. Again though, I haven't used it in a full campaign so I'm not 100% sure. For example it's true that if you're in Fire Aura you have access to Flickering Candle Meditation and Ember and Smoke Misdirection, which are both decent charms. You don't have access to Swaying Grass Elusion though, which is the only dodge charm that boosts your evasion cap. If you want to shed your Wood Aura for it it actually becomes twice as cheap as the Solar version of the same charm.<br /> <br /> So yes it is true that if you're a wood dragon dodger who likes to sit in wood aura you can't use Swaying Grass Elusion, and then counter with Unassailable Body of Fire. That's just, in theory anyway, the difference between how a wood dragon dodges and a fire dragon dodges. Or if you didn't want Swaying Grass you could still use Heat of Battle, Ebbing Tide, Flickering Candle, Hopping Firecracker, Virtious Negation and Bonfire Shadow Evasion. It's not strictly worse, but it is different, and it's a lot different from Solars and Lunars and stuff who can just combo anything they have.<br /> <br /> Also not that it matters for most games but at Essence 5 Elusive Dragon God Dispersion works sfor any element, and changes Unassailable Body of Fire and Hopping Firecracker to whatever element you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T10:15:17-07:00","id":1306273,"title":"","content":"I hate aura. It basically gives a middle finger to charms you want once you hit bonfire potentially locking you out of bonuses. The only way it'd work is if we had A LOT more charms than currently published. Maybe that will change with Heirs but I seriously doubt that as you'd need numbers exceeding Solar charms.<br /> <br /> Them and signature charms are my biggest gripes about DB's. Its supposed to function as a carrot but it feels more like getting clubbed on the back of the head. Even Elemental Surcharge in 2e was better than aura. The only reason I don't harp on it enough to make an essay on it is because I know the conditions Vinton had to do when Holdorke left, so the entire thing had to get out the door much less in an ideal platonic form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 04-20-2019, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T11:06:16-07:00","id":1306283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306273#post1306273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason I don't harp on it enough to make an essay on it is because I know the conditions Vinton had to do when Holdorke left, so the entire thing had to get out the door much less in an ideal platonic form.</div> </div> </div> </div>How charitable of you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T11:18:52-07:00","id":1306286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306193#post1306193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the third way is to try and make another element work outside of your own. Like you're a Fire aspect but you always take the Earth signature charms and be super careful about flaring your anima because it'll knock you out of the aura that you're in.<br /> <br /> Or some kind of weird advanced hybrid of all three where you use Earth charms until your anima flares, use some kind of Fire charm that expends your Aura and then fall back on mixing elements for the battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried doing this with a Water aspect using Melee mostly in Fire Aura and switching to Water Aura and Roaring River Slash for a finisher. My advice on that type of build? Don't. It fucking sucks.<br /> <br /> I stuck with that character for 20+ sessions and all the way up to Essence 3 (mostly because more than half his stuff was social and that part of him was really fun) but in the end I had to retire him. Now I'm playing a Martial Artist and using as few DB charms as possible (all in-element). So far it's working great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T11:45:43-07:00","id":1306294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306286#post1306286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried doing this with a Water aspect using Melee mostly in Fire Aura and switching to Water Aura and Roaring River Slash for a finisher. My advice on that type of build? Don't. It fucking sucks.<br /> <br /> I stuck with that character for 20+ sessions and all the way up to Essence 3 (mostly because more than half his stuff was social and that part of him was really fun) but in the end I had to retire him. Now I'm playing a Martial Artist and using as few DB charms as possible (all in-element). So far it's working great.</div> </div> </div> </div>What sucks about it? I might have to come up with a house rule or two for my group.<br /> <br /> Just to be more clear, I mean things like you found it hard to keep fire aura before your decisive, or there wasn\u2019t a good opportunity to spend motes to flare your anima prior to the hit, or like maybe you felt really restricted while you were in fire aura because you couldn\u2019t mix it with other aspect charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-20-2019, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:19:21-07:00","id":1306322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306268#post1306268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not actually sure if that's true, in all cases anyway. Again though, I haven't used it in a full campaign so I'm not 100% sure. For example it's true that if you're in Fire Aura you have access to Flickering Candle Meditation and Ember and Smoke Misdirection, which are both decent charms. You don't have access to Swaying Grass Elusion though, which is the only dodge charm that boosts your evasion cap. If you want to shed your Wood Aura for it it actually becomes twice as cheap as the Solar version of the same charm.<br /> <br /> So yes it is true that if you're a wood dragon dodger who likes to sit in wood aura you can't use Swaying Grass Elusion, and then counter with Unassailable Body of Fire. That's just, in theory anyway, the difference between how a wood dragon dodges and a fire dragon dodges. Or if you didn't want Swaying Grass you could still use Heat of Battle, Ebbing Tide, Flickering Candle, Hopping Firecracker, Virtious Negation and Bonfire Shadow Evasion. It's not strictly worse, but it is different, and it's a lot different from Solars and Lunars and stuff who can just combo anything they have.<br /> <br /> Also not that it matters for most games but at Essence 5 Elusive Dragon God Dispersion works sfor any element, and changes Unassailable Body of Fire and Hopping Firecracker to whatever element you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it wasn't strickly worse and it is because fire dodge has a bunch of tricks that use aura. Like you lose coiling dragon dance which is a major boost to the style. Even bigger than +2 cap evasion because it lets you actually get subtract from solars who can only reroll 1s and not 2s. That and it's basically 20% chance of stealing successes over 10%.<br /> <br /> Even then, It'd be easier for say a fire stylist to change swaying leaf evasion with a charm or evocation than it would be for the wood stylist to change the entire dodge tree.<br /> <br /> Also, the issue isn't just about being worse it's about the dragon blooded basically having dead charms in their charmset. Ones which stop higher level charms from functioning and rewarding optimization.<br /> <br /> Also, you should take a look at resistance. Several high essence charms require aura including the last one. The real kicker is that it's only e4 charm is in water aura and e5 charm is in air and requires the water charm. So earth aura use stops at e4 and air aura users have to buy a dead aura charm to get theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T14:21:07-07:00","id":1306336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306283#post1306283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How charitable of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe it or not I do have something resembling a heart in the black void within my chest. I am not like another individual who won't be named who only cares about the end product and endlessly harps on about it regardless of circumstances.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded we have now are good, the best one's we've ever had. 2e's charms were terrible and 1e was 1e. Are 3e Dragonblooded perfect? Hell no, there are what I consider to be several problems at the root level of DB's themselves, but are nothing that haven't been echo'd already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T15:06:22-07:00","id":1306342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306322#post1306322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if it wasn't strickly worse and it is because fire dodge has a bunch of tricks that use aura. Like you lose coiling dragon dance which is a major boost to the style. Even bigger than +2 cap evasion because it lets you actually get subtract from solars who can only reroll 1s and not 2s. That and it's basically 20% chance of stealing successes over 10%.<br /> <br /> Even then, It'd be easier for say a fire stylist to change swaying leaf evasion with a charm or evocation than it would be for the wood stylist to change the entire dodge tree.<br /> <br /> Also, the issue isn't just about being worse it's about the dragon blooded basically having dead charms in their charmset. Ones which stop higher level charms from functioning and rewarding optimization.<br /> <br /> Also, you should take a look at resistance. Several high essence charms require aura including the last one. The real kicker is that it's only e4 charm is in water aura and e5 charm is in air and requires the water charm. So earth aura use stops at e4 and air aura users have to buy a dead aura charm to get theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at resistance Hurricane Defense definitely should have just come off of Earth Bears Witness, I think. There\u2019s very few reasons for either of the two previous water charms to exist in your charm list if you\u2019re also trying to do air aura stuff.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not entirely convinced about dodge though, flickering candle only lets you ignore penalties to your Defense, which if there aren\u2019t any just isn\u2019t being used, where as a Wood Dragon can always cap burst her evasion. It\u2019s not better in every case, but if a Solar or Lunar is launching some big 32m 3wp decisive at you and you can bring your evasion up by 2 it\u2019s better to be a Wood Dragon in that case.<br /> <br /> Also as a Wood dragon your anima lets you ignore penalties to your evasion anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-20-2019, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T15:40:39-07:00","id":1306348,"title":"","content":"I will say that I hadn\u2019t seen the rule about Bonfire Anima at first, and I\u2019m not really sure why it\u2019s there.<br /> <br /> Still, Not hard to just... *nudges rule off the table onto the floor*<br /> <br /> And the thing is, it really is a good charmset. i would agree it\u2019s solidly the best shake DBs have gotten, not as a matter of power but in terms of theme and competencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-20-2019, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T16:19:20-07:00","id":1306355,"title":"","content":"I agree, I loved the elemental themes in DBs and in their charms. The Aspect bio's were pretty much some of my favorite parts of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T16:26:10-07:00","id":1306358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306342#post1306342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking at resistance Hurricane Defense definitely should have just come off of Earth Bears Witness, I think. There\u2019s very few reasons for either of the two previous water charms to exist in your charm list if you\u2019re also trying to do air aura stuff.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not entirely convinced about dodge though, flickering candle only lets you ignore penalties to your Defense, which if there aren\u2019t any just isn\u2019t being used, where as a Wood Dragon can always cap burst her evasion. It\u2019s not better in every case, but if a Solar or Lunar is launching some big 32m 3wp decisive at you and you can bring your evasion up by 2 it\u2019s better to be a Wood Dragon in that case.<br /> <br /> Also as a Wood dragon your anima lets you ignore penalties to your evasion anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bigger deal is bonfire flicker evasion and the ability to deal with withering but you'd have to keep being at bonfire to keep aura up.<br /> <br /> Yeah decisive up front is a thing but +2 wouldn't help you anyway. And if they're doing it on the first turn of combat you'd be screwed anyway because you don't have an aura up and if you don't have an aura up you can't use it all. Like Dragon blooded already had restrictions built in and it doesn't feel, at least to me, that aura does anything but hinder someone who wants to combine abilities together in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T17:47:47-07:00","id":1306369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306358#post1306358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger deal is bonfire flicker evasion and the ability to deal with withering but you'd have to keep being at bonfire to keep aura up.<br /> <br /> Yeah decisive up front is a thing but +2 wouldn't help you anyway. And if they're doing it on the first turn of combat you'd be screwed anyway because you don't have an aura up and if you don't have an aura up you can't use it all. Like Dragon blooded already had restrictions built in and it doesn't feel, at least to me, that aura does anything but hinder someone who wants to combine most abilities together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow, I didn't even realize it also affected Bonfire Shadow Evasion, that's a neat trick. That actually could also be a cool way to knock yourself OUT of bonfire, and thus be able to enter into other auras again. The +2 from Swaying Grass IS still really helpful though, against decisive attacks it can definitely make the difference, it won't always of course, but a lot of the time. Especially since as a DB if the only people you're facing in combat are heavily optimized Dawn casts you've either entered into a more rare sort of game or have a ST that's kind of a dick.<br /> <br /> If the aura mechanic didn't exist though, you could actually combine Coiling Dragon with Bonfire Shadow Evasion and Swaying Grass Elusion and possibly even Safety Among Enemies, which is really powerful, and maybe a bit too powerful for what Dragonblooded are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Some of it, too, is just playing different aspects in different ways. Like Earth doesn't have a single Dodge charm apart from the sig, and eventually at Essence 5 Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, Hopping Firecracker Evasion and Unassailable Body of Fire. On the flip side though Resistance doesn't have a single fire charm except for the sig, and a few charms that can be any element, none of which give you bonus soak or anything like that. Then you also have things like the Whirlwind Shield Technique int Vengeful Gust Counterattack into Wind Armor Technique.<br /> <br /> I like it personally, or at least in theory I do, I'll have to see after starting a game myself or doing more just DB test combats, but I can see why other people might not like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:12:00-07:00","id":1306372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306369#post1306369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh wow, I didn't even realize it also affected Bonfire Shadow Evasion, that's a neat trick. That actually could also be a cool way to knock yourself OUT of bonfire, and thus be able to enter into other auras again. The +2 from Swaying Grass IS still really helpful though, against decisive attacks it can definitely make the difference, it won't always of course, but a lot of the time. Especially since as a DB if the only people you're facing in combat are heavily optimized Dawn casts you've either entered into a more rare sort of game or have a ST that's kind of a dick.<br /> <br /> If the aura mechanic didn't exist though, you could actually combine Coiling Dragon with Bonfire Shadow Evasion and Swaying Grass Elusion and possibly even Safety Among Enemies, which is really powerful, and maybe a bit too powerful for what Dragonblooded are supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>As fun as that'd be. It's pretty impossible. Even without Aura, signature style charms are limited to one purchase at E3 and one at E5. Personally, I don't disagree with aura in theory but the charmsets that require aura need to be about 4x what they to compensate for the issues. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, each element should have had a form of attack and a form of defense and they should have all been a single element. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of it, too, is just playing different aspects in different ways. Like Earth doesn't have a single Dodge charm apart from the sig, and eventually at Essence 5 Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, Hopping Firecracker Evasion and Unassailable Body of Fire. On the flip side though Resistance doesn't have a single fire charm except for the sig, and a few charms that can be any element, none of which give you bonus soak or anything like that. Then you also have things like the Whirlwind Shield Technique int Vengeful Gust Counterattack into Wind Armor Technique. </div> </div> </div>That's what my problem is. It feels a little unfair that some combinations have huge advantages but others don't.<br /> <br /> Also, I just found out that Dragon-Blooded brawl was water bending as was the signature charm which works with MA. So now I'm kind of a little miffed that my character wouldn't really work with a switch to a water DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:29:36-07:00","id":1306383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306372#post1306372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As fun as that'd be. It's pretty impossible. Even without Aura, signature style charms are limited to one purchase at E3 and one at E5. Personally, I don't disagree with aura in theory but the charmsets that require aura need to be about 4x what they to compensate for the issues. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, each element should have had a form of attack and a form of defense and they should have all been a single element. <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might put them a bit above where Dragonblooded are supposed to be strength wise. If we\u2019re talking about Essence 4-5 charms though Dragon God makes a few other charms any element.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t quite understand your second paragraph here though, like there should have been pure element trees?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306372#post1306372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what my problem is. It feels a little unfair that some combinations have huge advantages but others don't.<br /> <br /> Also, I just found out that Dragon-Blooded brawl was water bending as was the signature charm which works with MA. So now I'm kind of a little miffed that my character wouldn't really work with a switch to a water DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m also not sure what you\u2019re saying here either. Maybe the kind of character you want is just a Solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:39:28-07:00","id":1306384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306383#post1306383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that might put them a bit above where Dragonblooded are supposed to be strength wise. If we\u2019re talking about Essence 4-5 charms though Dragon God makes a few other charms any element.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so. They are already pretty balanced towards the level they're supposed to be even with persistent aura use. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t quite understand your second paragraph here though, like there should have been pure element trees? </div> </div> </div>Yes. With signature charms just being limited by aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m also not sure what you\u2019re saying here either. Maybe the kind of character you want is just a Solar? </div> </div> </div>No. I have a character from an upcoming terrestrial game. The way my character fights will use a combination of presence + Dodge + Dragon fire style. One that uses charms like moth to flame to get attacked. The only issue is that I kind of want to do it as a water dragon DB but can't because those charms are specifically fire aspected and that prevents other charms from working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T19:11:43-07:00","id":1306390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306384#post1306384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe so. They are already pretty balanced towards the level they're supposed to be even with persistent aura use. <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. With signature charms just being limited by aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but if they\u2019re 4X, as powerful that would be way too much.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m maybe still not quite getting it. So do away with them being based on abilities and doing pure element, like how Lunars have charm trees based on Dex DBs would just have a Fire tree?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306384#post1306384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I have a character from an upcoming terrestrial game. The way my character fights will use a combination of presence + Dodge + Dragon fire style. One that uses charms like moth to flame to get attacked. The only issue is that I kind of want to do it as a water dragon DB but can't because those charms are specifically fire aspected and that prevents other charms from working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I see. Yeah that\u2019s just not easy to do. If you\u2019re using so much fire though, with three heavy fire aspected abilities including the dragon style, what\u2019s driving you to be a Water aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T19:35:46-07:00","id":1306394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306390#post1306390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right but if they\u2019re 4X, as powerful that would be way too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say 4x as powerful though I said 4x as big. So every element has proper elemental trees in each ability. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah I see. Yeah that\u2019s just not easy to do. If you\u2019re using so much fire though, with three heavy fire aspected abilities including the dragon style, what\u2019s driving you to be a Water aspect? </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea would have been the same it's just Instead of dodge I would use a combination of brawl crane and MA. Brawl would honestly be just two dip in charms. But hmm. I wonder, if I can use an evocation to change the element of moth to the flame I can still do what I want. Hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:02:17-07:00","id":1306397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306294#post1306294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sucks about it? I might have to come up with a house rule or two for my group.<br /> <br /> Just to be more clear, I mean things like you found it hard to keep fire aura before your decisive, or there wasn\u2019t a good opportunity to spend motes to flare your anima prior to the hit, or like maybe you felt really restricted while you were in fire aura because you couldn\u2019t mix it with other aspect charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you have to carefully micromagane your Anima level and thus your mote expenditure. Not only do you have to avoid going bonfire too early, but since there aren't any Water Melee charms that you can activate on your turn (the only one being a parry charm) going bonfire is virtually the only realiable method you have of entering Water Aura. So you have to float at Anima level 2 and time it just right to flare iconic right before you drop the decisive. If anything messes with that gameplan (and EVERYTHING will mess it up: forced to full excellency parry to avoid going splat? lost your Aura. Whiffed the Decisive? lost your Aura. Landed the decisive but the target survives/there are other targets? lost your Aura) well you're stuck in Water Aura now so good luck fighting the rest of the scene with half your charms turned off.<br /> <br /> The other half of the problem is that because my game-plan was based around eventually hardlocking into Water Aura that meant I was heavily de-incentivised from taking non-essential charms that were non-balanced or aura-keyworded. That meant no Flame Warden Stance, no Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite, etc. And it turns out all of the fun Fire stuff, the stuff that changes your gameplay and gives you unique strategies and options (reflexive clashes, non-resetting decisives, ranged attacks, flurries, status effects, etc.) ALL come at Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Meaning that for several months of playing the game my combat flowchart was:<br /> walk up to enemy =&gt; withering w/excellency =&gt; is it crash? if no step 2 again, if yes =&gt; full excellency decisive =&gt;is it dead? if yes go back to step 1, if no cry for party members to save me cause I can't do shit.<br /> If I got attacked I either parried with the excellency or face-tanked it with my artifact armor. Blazing Interception is almost never worth it so after a while I stopped using it altogether. Best defense against decisives that didn't fuck up my Aura was Wound-Denying Dragon Faith and a shit-ton of OX Bodies.<br /> <br /> The build was quite effective (only really thwarted by soak-monsters due to a lack of withering damage enhancers or alternative ways of gaining initiative) but it was incredibly dull to play, with barely any meaningful decision-making.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile I was looking at my Fire-Aspected Hearthmate who was far less invested in combat than I was, who went freely around tossing Melee (fire) charms, then when her initiative was deemed good enough she would reposition using Athletics (also fire) charms to get a good angle and then unleash TERRYFYING ROAR OF THE FIRE DRAGON (also a fire charm obviously) and win the fight. And her player never had to worry about anything: my aspect is fire, all of my charms are fire charms, my aura is always fire, I flare my anima whenever I fucking want, and my finishing move is the only charm I have that requires expending aura and I'm always in fire aura so it's always ready to go. Even my fucking social charms are fire charms. So yeah, you can tell why I was a bit jealous.<br /> <br /> /end rant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":10131,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","user":"BadassOverlord","date":". 04-20-2019, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:23:50-07:00","id":1306401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306397#post1306397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile I was looking at my Fire-Aspected Hearthmate who was far less invested in combat than I was, who went freely around tossing Melee (fire) charms, then when her initiative was deemed good enough she would reposition using Athletics (also fire) charms to get a good angle and then unleash TERRYFYING ROAR OF THE FIRE DRAGON (also a fire charm obviously) and win the fight. And her player never had to worry about anything: my aspect is fire, all of my charms are fire charms, my aura is always fire, I flare my anima whenever I fucking want, and my finishing move is the only charm I have that requires expending aura and I'm always in fire aura so it's always ready to go. Even my fucking social charms are fire charms. So yeah, you can tell why I was a bit jealous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is what I was talking about. I noticed fire has amazing synergy but other elements weren't as lucky when it comes to combat. I also noticed that combat's the only time aura is really an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:28:46-07:00","id":1306402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306372#post1306372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, each element should have had a form of attack and a form of defense and they should have all been a single element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrown (Air) and Archery (Wood) depend on distance for defense. Thrown also has defensive Air Charms, and Archery has defensive Wood Charms.<br /> <br /> Stealth Charms offer another form of defense for Thrown specialists, and most of its Charms are also Air-aspected. Ride Charms offer another form of defense for Archery specialists, and most of its Charms are also Wood-aspected.<br /> <br /> Brawl (Water) has Water Charms for parrying and for grappling (which hinders or outright prevents the target from attacking).<br /> <br /> Elusive Crosswind Defense is an Air Dodge Charm that works best at distances, so someone using Thrown Charms to build up an Air Aura has the perfect Dodge Charm to use. Safety Among Enemies can work at any range, including against ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> Swaying Grass Elusion works well at any range, but definitely helps when you're caught at close range with only a bow (and you might not have Wood Dragon Style for parrying), and certainly helps avoid ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> Ebbing Tide Recedes is a nice complement to the Water Aspect anima power, and the Water-aspected movement-generating Charms in Brawl. Brawl also has Water-aspected Charms to attack from range. Flow With Strife works well with the Water-aspected Resistance Charms that help reduce the amount of damage you might suffer from getting hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:34:09-07:00","id":1306403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306402#post1306402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thrown (Air) and Archery (Wood) depend on distance for defense. Thrown also has defensive Air Charms, and Archery has defensive Wood Charms.<br /> <br /> Stealth Charms offer another form of defense for Thrown specialists, and most of its Charms are also Air-aspected. Ride Charms offer another form of defense for Archery specialists, and most of its Charms are also Wood-aspected.<br /> <br /> Brawl (Water) has Water Charms for parrying and for grappling (which hinders or outright prevents the target from attacking).<br /> <br /> Elusive Crosswind Defense is an Air Dodge Charm that works best at distances, so someone using Thrown Charms to build up an Air Aura has the perfect Dodge Charm to use. Safety Among Enemies can work at any range, including against ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> Swaying Grass Elusion works well at any range, but definitely helps when you're caught at close range with only a bow (and you might not have Wood Dragon Style for parrying), and certainly helps avoid ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> Ebbing Tide Recedes is a nice complement to the Water Aspect anima power, and the Water-aspected movement-generating Charms in Brawl. Brawl also has Water-aspected Charms to attack from range. Flow With Strife works well with the Water-aspected Resistance Charms that help reduce the amount of damage you might suffer from getting hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not disagreeing but I do feel it's a little different than the aspects who have the a majority of the defense trees and bread and butter techniques. It seems to be an issue IMO to have a system like this and give Fire both dodge and melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-20-2019, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:52:40-07:00","id":1306408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306403#post1306403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing but I do feel it's a little different than the aspects who have the a majority of the defense trees and bread and butter techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm not about to say that the Terrestrial Charmset is perfect.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why the pinnacle Resistance Charm is Air-aspected and requires an Air Aura, when the only Resistance Charms for building an Air Aura is a specific application of Body-Cleansing Prana.<br /> <br /> Now, it makes sense that the Air Signature Resistance Charm requires an Air Aura, because plenty of Signatures are useful (or accessible) only for Dragon-Blooded of the same Aspect, and anyone can grab a Signature Charm without buying any other Charm from the same Ability.<br /> <br /> But how many Air Aspects are really going to invest so heavily into RESISTANCE Charms? Between Stealth, ranged Thrown attacks, ranged Thrown defenses, ranged Sorcery spells, ranged Lore attacks, the Air Anima effects for defending against ranged attacks and leaping up into the safety of high places... HOW MANY Air Aspects are going to invest so deeply into Resistance?!<br /> <br /> Why reward those few Air Aspects instead of supporting the larger number of Earth, Water, and Wood Aspects who use Brawl to fight?<br /> <br /> At least Ripples-on-Water Defense and Flowing Dragon-Body Endurance make some sense, since many Earth Aspects (and not a few Wood Aspects) are Brawl specialists and might use those Charms to build up a Water Aura, and these two Charms definitely help out the Water Aspect Brawl specialists.<br /> <br /> Earth Bears Witness can be either Earth (like the rest of Resistance) or Water (again, useful for Brawl specialists).<br /> <br /> Supple Viridian Scales makes sense for a Wood Aspect who decided to invest in Resisance and armor, since it helps them ignore mobility penalties for disengaging to Archery range. Or when rushing an opponent to use Wood-aspected Brawl Charms. Or dodging with Swaying Grass Evasion when caught at close range and wearing armor.<br /> <br /> Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit is of limited use to non-Fire Aspects, and locks Fire Aspects out of virtually all Resistance Charms, rewarding a Fire Aspect who can rely on Dodge or Melee parry Charms for defense. Which, fair enough, they alone can do while remaining entirely within their native Aura.<br /> <br /> But the pinnacle Charm? Makes no sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-20-2019, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T21:03:43-07:00","id":1306419,"title":"","content":"I think when your concept is a specialist with an aspect that isn\u2019t prominent in their specialty (say, a Wood Meleeist), you\u2019re essentially coming up against the same problem as a demon summoner who doesn\u2019t want to summon Blood Apes, Agata, or Neomah. <br /> <br /> Or like, any character with an original artifact.<br /> You might have to write the charms yourself. Which I get isn\u2019t ideal, but it is solidly expected in ex3 for many character concepts.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn\u2019t want the abilities to be element specific, and I wouldn\u2019t ask for the charmset to be a full two thirds of a significantly larger book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T21:11:25-07:00","id":1306420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306419#post1306419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think when your concept is a specialist with an aspect that isn\u2019t prominent in their specialty (say, a Wood Meleeist), you\u2019re essentially coming up against the same problem as a demon summoner who doesn\u2019t want to summon Blood Apes, Agata, or Neomah.<br /> <br /> Or like, any character with an original artifact.<br /> You might have to write the charms yourself. Which I get isn\u2019t ideal, but it is solidly expected in ex3 for many character concepts.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn\u2019t want the abilities to be element specific, and I wouldn\u2019t ask for the charmset to be a full two thirds of a significantly larger book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's kind of an incorrect analogy. This is like a demon summoner having to chose between summoning a blood ape, agata or neomah and then getting locked out summoning the other two. And while I don't have a problem writing my own charms, It's hard to understand to understand the intent behind aura or what was left out of chopping block and what shouldn't be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T23:04:13-07:00","id":1306441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306394#post1306394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say 4x as powerful though I said 4x as big. So every element has proper elemental trees in each ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, the idea would have been the same it's just Instead of dodge I would use a combination of brawl crane and MA. Brawl would honestly be just two dip in charms. But hmm. I wonder, if I can use an evocation to change the element of moth to the flame I can still do what I want. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let's figure out what you're trying to do here and maybe we can work something with minimal homebrew required. Not that homebrew is bad, it's just work. So you want to be able to taunt enemies and tank for the party basically?<br /> <br /> One thing I notice is that Moth to the Candle is just a simple charm that you only need to use once right when the battle starts, so it's element matters a lot less. It's not like it has &quot;Duration: Aura&quot; or anything like that. Crane would be a great style to use with that, since all Crane wants to do is take Full Defense actions and counter attack. Rather than Brawl though I actually think you could go for Water Dragon. Its first charm lets you flurry a full defense with an attack action, so you're actually getting to attack while using Crane style, which normally you don't get to do, and they're water charms that harmonize with your anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T23:39:47-07:00","id":1306448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306397#post1306397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SNIP<br /> /end rant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems really strange to me. Sorry, maybe I'm just not reading you right but Blinding Spark Distraction and Crossfire Flash are also both balanced, and they give some cool options, you can try to delay and clash to get some free non-charm dice, or blind an opponent without screwing up your Water Aura. Also if you took Dragon Graced Weapon it gives your sword the Flexible and Grappling tags, the former is really situational and honestly you'll probably forget you have it when you actually need to use it, but making your sword a grappling weapon opens up a host of options for you.<br /> <br /> Even if you zero dotes in Brawl or a Martial Art, grappling can still be great. As long as you hit, and make the difficulty 2 roll, you don't have to win the control roll, you always get at least one turn, which can include a withering savage against an enemy with defense 0 against your daiklave attack. Also, again even if you totally fail, you're holding them and penalizing their defense until your target acts again.<br /> <br /> You could even do all of them at once, delay to clash their attack with your own decisive grapple attempt, win the clash because of Crossfire Flash, and blind your target, which might even them a penalty on their grapple roll, so that's good. Even if it doesn't though, you're not going to launch that attack unless you have like 8 initiative ready to easily make that gambit roll of difficulty 2. Then you get your sweet free grappling savage, and for all your circlemates this guy now has a -3 or -4 penalty directly to their defense. So that's pretty good.<br /> <br /> In fact if you had Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode, and either hadn't gone totemic yet or just didn't mind losing your aura, you wouldn't even have to wait. I'm not exactly sure on the rules for this but you might even be able to use your action to aim, then reflexively comet deflecting mode, clash with a BUNCH of bonus dice, even more than your weapon normally adds for accuracy, and use THAT to go totemic, binding them into a grapple and savaging them for a boat ton of initiative and then on your next turn unleash Roaring River Slash.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, sure, doing the withering attack into anima-flare roaring river slash it one option, but it's hardly your only one in a fight.<br /> <br /> Also, once you get it of course, Cloud Riot adds a whole new dimension to the whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T23:49:09-07:00","id":1306451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306441#post1306441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So let's figure out what you're trying to do here and maybe we can work something with minimal homebrew required. Not that homebrew is bad, it's just work. So you want to be able to taunt enemies and tank for the party basically?<br /> <br /> One thing I notice is that Moth to the Candle is just a simple charm that you only need to use once right when the battle starts, so it's element matters a lot less. It's not like it has &quot;Duration: Aura&quot; or anything like that. Crane would be a great style to use with that, since all Crane wants to do is take Full Defense actions and counter attack. Rather than Brawl though I actually think you could go for Water Dragon. Its first charm lets you flurry a full defense with an attack action, so you're actually getting to attack while using Crane style, which normally you don't get to do, and they're water charms that harmonize with your anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I already know what I want to do. I think you think these two seperate thoughs are the same but they aren't. Like I already have a build and a few custom charms planned for it. My character is a fire aspected dragon blooded. His aura use is pretty much 100%.<br /> <br /> My issue with aura is how 100% aura use is limited to like 2-3 builds without extremely heavy homebrew and also that dragon blooded have to buy dead charms. Like 2e had a massive issues with filler charms but DB's sometimes have to buy charms that absolutely cannot work for their build. I just feel aura was mishandled in that several other archetypes get screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-21-2019, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T23:58:10-07:00","id":1306453,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to use defensive charms to get into aura anyway, since they tend to get used outside ones turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T00:12:11-07:00","id":1306457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306451#post1306451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I already know what I want to do. I think you think these two seperate thoughs are the same but they aren't. Like I already have a build and a few custom charms planned for it. My character is a fire aspected dragon blooded. His aura use is pretty much 100%.<br /> <br /> My issue with aura is how 100% aura use is limited to like 2-3 builds without extremely heavy homebrew and also that dragon blooded have to buy dead charms. Like 2e had a massive issues with filler charms but DB's sometimes have to buy charms that absolutely cannot work for their build. I just feel aura was mishandled in that several other archetypes get screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh okay I see, sorry I thought when you said you wanted an evocation that changes the element of Moth to Candle it was because you weren't using Fire.<br /> <br /> I do think that some builds got screwed, or are just too difficult to pull off. Like if you wanted to be an Earth Aspect who uses dodge offensively like Fire Aspects can do, or wanted to be an Air and get a bunch of ox-bodies so you can just sit in Unfeeling Earth Meditation and not even care that she's in her -2s all the time. It just doesn't work, you NEED to be the right aspect for those kind of builds, and make sure to use combat charms that are in line with that aspect as well. For those kind of things you get pigeonholed into your aspect. Which does suck.<br /> <br /> Even Solars can suffer that problem, like if I wanted to be the greatest swordsman ever, and use that skill in the name of the Sun, to be his priest and his avenging blade in the world...I can't be a Zenith. I WANT to be the ultimate warrior priest-paladin, but I need to be a Dawn for that. Otherwise I'm stuck with Essence 1 charms and watching my Dawn circlemate run rings around me in combat, even though my concept is to be just as great.<br /> <br /> There are some cool out of-aspect things that you can do though. Like if you're an Earth Aspect who does Dodge and Archery. Those aren't abilities you generally think of as being Earth-y. BUT their two signatures mesh really well, by forcing enemies away from you, into your bow's optimal range, and then letting you decisively counterattack them if they strike you from there, and all targeting an opponent's resolve to do it. OR since Earth's Judgement isn't Aura keyworded, and explicitly works with charms like Hopping Firecracker Evasion, she can do cool stuff like dodge in close range, hop out to optimal bow range and then fire a parting counter attack as she goes. It's cool, and something that Fire aspects can't do, in spite of Fire being the masters of dodge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T00:19:08-07:00","id":1306458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306457#post1306457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\<br /> Even Solars can suffer that problem, like if I wanted to be the greatest swordsman ever, and use that skill in the name of the Sun, to be his priest and his avenging blade in the world...I can't be a Zenith. I WANT to be the ultimate warrior priest-paladin, but I need to be a Dawn for that. Otherwise I'm stuck with Essence 1 charms and watching my Dawn circlemate run rings around me in combat, even though my concept is to be just as great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is different. Because eventually you'll get the charms to match him just using the book. Dragon-blooded get locked out of charms and some trees have aura so often that you have to buy heavily incompatible charms. Every charm a solar has can always be used unconditionally no matter the circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:14:35-07:00","id":1306468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306458#post1306458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is different. Because eventually you'll get the charms to match him just using the book. Dragon-blooded get locked out of charms and some trees have aura so often that you have to buy heavily incompatible charms. Every charm a solar has can always be used unconditionally no matter the circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is different in that way, but it still has the game holding up a hand and telling you that no, you have to wait for 310xp before you can use Circle of Bright Reaving. You do eventually get it, but you'll never have a supernal Melee Zenith.<br /> <br /> There are some bad Aura placed charms, I think, that force you to buy charms that you shouldn't, and that is bad. You shouldn't be left with like 3 charms on your character sheet that require Water Aura to get to a cool Earth Aura charm for your Earth Aspect. That's just no good. It <i>certainly </i>isn't perfect.<br /> <br /> The part that I don't think is bad though is that some stuff needs a particular aura and makes things incompatible. Like how it gives Earth Aspects a totally different take on the Brawl tree, which is really well designed. Every Earth charm has a prerequisite of either Earth or a Balanced charm, so if you want you can pick up everything and still be 100% earth, and it gives you some powerful options to strike, smash and fling opponents across the battlefield in ways that a Water aspect just can't do easily. That's just Earth's way of doing Bawl and if you want to do it as a Water aspect it's extremely hard to do.<br /> <br /> It's also good to remember that Aura isn't like the be-all and end-all of Dragonblooded power either. There's tons of things you can do that just mix up all the elements freely and never worry about engaging with the Aura mechanic at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T02:41:42-07:00","id":1306483,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure we can really complain about castes or aspects having mechanical heft that limits character options. That's kind of... what they're supposed to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T02:59:10-07:00","id":1306486,"title":"","content":"I mean, yes, but also I houserule Supernal to be from any caste abilities because no one can convince me that only Eclipses can be supernally puissant pirates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:11:08-07:00","id":1306490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306468#post1306468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some bad Aura placed charms, I think, that force you to buy charms that you shouldn't, and that is bad. You shouldn't be left with like 3 charms on your character sheet that require Water Aura to get to a cool Earth Aura charm for your Earth Aspect. That's just no good. It <i>certainly </i>isn't perfect.<br /> <br /> The part that I don't think is bad though is that some stuff needs a particular aura and makes things incompatible. Like how it gives Earth Aspects a totally different take on the Brawl tree, which is really well designed. Every Earth charm has a prerequisite of either Earth or a Balanced charm, so if you want you can pick up everything and still be 100% earth, and it gives you some powerful options to strike, smash and fling opponents across the battlefield in ways that a Water aspect just can't do easily. That's just Earth's way of doing Bawl and if you want to do it as a Water aspect it's extremely hard to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a very good summary. In some ways, the aura and elemental charms work very well, with different Aspects being able to use the same Ability in their own unique way. Earth-Brawl is a good example, as is Fire-Archery, etc.<br /> <br /> But in some parts you have one Aspect buying 4 of one element and then the next element is different, and it's quite disruptive and awkward using them together.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is kind of deliberate; the point is you can use all your charms, but it's difficult to combo them. But in practice it can be a bit annoying.*<br /> <br /> *I think. I haven't played a Dragonblood. Some of my friends told me it was a bit annoying, others said it was fine. I don't know if this is due to their character builds or their different level of skill with game mechanics.<br /> Certainly the one DB I play alongside, the player find the incompatibility of Melee and Martial Arts more awkward than Aura.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:29:42-07:00","id":1306492,"title":"","content":"Ok, two things...<br /> <br /> One, Dragon kin Empowerment is cool, and could have some cool effects, the million dollar question being whether using a reflexive charm with an element during turn you enact it as a simple action will give you aura next turn. OR whether a reflexive charm taken Not On your turn can create or end Aura.<br /> <br /> Because two: RAW specifies that charms of the same aspect taken During your combat turn will create Aura. Which excludes like, all defensive charms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it specifies that a charm of a different aspect used at ANY time ends Aura, but doesn\u2019t specify that it Prevents an Aura from forming.<br /> <br /> Which means you Can use Fire parrying charms before unleashing Mela\u2019s death charm of murder. But only in between the turn in which you use only air charms and the turn in which you will form Aura.<br /> <br /> I feel like this can\u2019t possibly be intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T06:25:45-07:00","id":1306521,"title":"","content":"Check with Vance.<br /> <br /> It seems weird to me too, but it also how it reads to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T07:25:09-07:00","id":1306523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306457#post1306457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Solars can suffer that problem, like if I wanted to be the greatest swordsman ever, and use that skill in the name of the Sun, to be his priest and his avenging blade in the world...I can't be a Zenith. I WANT to be the ultimate warrior priest-paladin, but I need to be a Dawn for that. Otherwise I'm stuck with Essence 1 charms and watching my Dawn circlemate run rings around me in combat, even though my concept is to be just as great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to derail the topic here but if this is your concept maybe you should just play a Dawn instead of a Zenith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:24:38-07:00","id":1306542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306492#post1306492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, two things...<br /> <br /> One, Dragon kin Empowerment is cool, and could have some cool effects, the million dollar question being whether using a reflexive charm with an element during turn you enact it as a simple action will give you aura next turn. OR whether a reflexive charm taken Not On your turn can create or end Aura.<br /> <br /> Because two: RAW specifies that charms of the same aspect taken During your combat turn will create Aura. Which excludes like, all defensive charms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it specifies that a charm of a different aspect used at ANY time ends Aura, but doesn\u2019t specify that it Prevents an Aura from forming.<br /> <br /> Which means you Can use Fire parrying charms before unleashing Mela\u2019s death charm of murder. But only in between the turn in which you use only air charms and the turn in which you will form Aura.<br /> <br /> I feel like this can\u2019t possibly be intended.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> People have asked before; Charms used during your turn can generate Aura, disrupt ongoing Aura, and prevent Aura from forming. Charms used outside your turn cannot generate Aura. I would advise ignoring this since otherwise a lot of Charms like the Water Melee Signature become unusable barring some weird ass investment elsewhere or Custom Melee/Other Ability Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:28:42-07:00","id":1306543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306492#post1306492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, two things...<br /> <br /> One, Dragon kin Empowerment is cool, and could have some cool effects, the million dollar question being whether using a reflexive charm with an element during turn you enact it as a simple action will give you aura next turn. OR whether a reflexive charm taken Not On your turn can create or end Aura.<br /> <br /> Because two: RAW specifies that charms of the same aspect taken During your combat turn will create Aura. Which excludes like, all defensive charms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it specifies that a charm of a different aspect used at ANY time ends Aura, but doesn\u2019t specify that it Prevents an Aura from forming.<br /> <br /> Which means you Can use Fire parrying charms before unleashing Mela\u2019s death charm of murder. But only in between the turn in which you use only air charms and the turn in which you will form Aura.<br /> <br /> I feel like this can\u2019t possibly be intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure I get what you\u2019re saying here. If you only use charms of one element during your turn, then at the end of your turn you enter that aura. So, say, you act on initiative 8. When initiative 8 comes around if you use Air aspected Elemental Bolt Attack, then when initiative 7 rolls around you\u2019re in air aura. If you then get attacked on initiative 5 and use Hopping Firecracker as part of your Defense, you lose the air aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:40:04-07:00","id":1306549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306542#post1306542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> People have asked before; Charms used during your turn can generate Aura, disrupt ongoing Aura, and prevent Aura from forming. Charms used outside your turn cannot generate Aura. I would advise ignoring this since otherwise a lot of Charms like the Water Melee Signature become unusable barring some weird ass investment elsewhere or Custom Melee/Other Ability Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really? That\u2019s odd. I\u2019m not sure if I like that or not. On the one hand it lets you mix up defensive charms freely without compromising your ability to enter an aura, on the other hand yeah it definitely does make entering things like water aura before you get to bonfire a lot harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:46:31-07:00","id":1306552,"title":"","content":"There's a reflexive 1m water Awareness charm. I think that's the best way to get into Water Aura as a Melee-ist.<br /> Seems a little silly, admittedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:04:26-07:00","id":1306558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306549#post1306549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh really? That\u2019s odd. I\u2019m not sure if I like that or not. On the one hand it lets you mix up defensive charms freely without compromising your ability to enter an aura, on the other hand yeah it definitely does make entering things like water aura before you get to bonfire a lot harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>That gives you an extremely huge advantage in that case.There are a number of Aura long defensive charms that can combine with non-aura charms. It is gaming the system but it does help people who want to use off aura abilities and not lose things. It doesn't get rid of all my problems with the system but it does help. I guess that's why dodge doesn't have a single balance charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:04:26-07:00","id":1306559,"title":"","content":"Double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:31:34-07:00","id":1306565,"title":"","content":"Be water aspect.<br /> Use a cantrip stunt and balanced charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:37:16-07:00","id":1306568,"title":"","content":"I'm still stuck on Terrestrial Resistance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Resistance is the Earth Aspect's defensive Ability. They don't have Dodge, Ride, or Melee, and the Earth-aspected Charms in Brawl don't include any parrying Charms. But Resistance seems reluctant to serve the Earth Aspect.<br /> <br /> What good does an Earth Aura do for you, with this Ability's Charms? It's great with Impervious Skin of Stone, especially if you want to use Balanced Dodge Charms and keep ISoS in reserve in case you fail to evade. It lets you use the basic Earth version of Earth Bears Witness. It lets you use Perfected Scales of the Dragon, but that's a double-edged Charm.<br /> <br /> But all of the strongest Charms of this Ability require non-Earth Auras!<br /> <br /> <br /> Resistance seems to better serve Water Aspects, since they can use Impervious Skin of Stone <i>and </i>Eternal Tide Endurance together without losing Water Aura, and having a Water Aura lets them use the Water version of Earth Bears Witness, as well as the penultimate Charms of Ripples-on-Water Defense and Flowing Dragon-Body Endurance. Fathomless Depths Replenishment is best used outside of a fight and thus doesn't benefit from or threaten any Aura.<br /> <br /> Sure, Earth Aspects can gain some defense from being distant from targets while using Earth-aspected Thrown Charms, but Water Aspects can enjoy even better range with the Water-aspected Archery Charms!<br /> <br /> Is the 5m, Until Next Turn soak/hardness bonus of the Earth Anima Effect enough to make up for this disparity?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense... Even if you're an Air Aspect who can simply get an Air Aura by having any Aura and going bonfire, the easiest way to generate the Air Aura that this Resistance pinnacle Charm needs is to invest in Thrown Charms.<br /> <br /> If you're investing in Thrown Charms, at the same Essence level, you can learn Whirlwind Shield Technique. Then, rather than investing in the Resistance Ability to begin learning Resistance Charms, you could continue investing in Thrown to buy Vengeful Gust Counterstrike, and then farther still with Wind Armor Technique, WHICH IS INCOMPATIBLE WITH ARMOR.<br /> <br /> Before getting RHFD, if you're using Thrown Charms to build and exploit an Air Aura, and want to keep that Aura, you can only use Impervious Skin of Stone, and you can't even enjoy the Earth Aura bonus of that Charm.<br /> <br /> You can only use Eternal Tide Endurance, Supple Viridian Scales, or Immovable Mountain Technique if you're okay with losing Air Aura.<br /> <br /> You can't use at all any version of Earth Bears Witness, Ripples-on-Water Defense, or Flowing Dragon-Body Endurance, since they all require non-Air Auras. At least you can use RHFD initially and then afterwards switch to generating and using Auras of other elements.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, no, RHFD has a duration of Aura. If you lose that Air Aura, you lose the protection. This not only prevents stacking its effects with any Resistance Charms other than Impervious Skin of Stone and Body-Like-Clouds Meditation, it also makes it that much harder to use together with Whirlwind Shield Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-21-2019, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:17:01-07:00","id":1306579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306549#post1306549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh really? That\u2019s odd. I\u2019m not sure if I like that or not. On the one hand it lets you mix up defensive charms freely without compromising your ability to enter an aura, on the other hand yeah it definitely does make entering things like water aura before you get to bonfire a lot harder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It lets you mix up defensive Charms freely as long as you don't mind getting immediately thrown out of Aura and not having Aura during your next turn, which is kind of the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T12:14:04-07:00","id":1306603,"title":"","content":"(Ahk I was wrong about when Aura starts, my mistake)<br /> Ok yeah, without between-turn reflexives, Aura becomes ridiculous. Basically if you don\u2019t have everyone take Dragon-kin empowerment, you should ignore any charm that isn\u2019t your aspect.<br /> <br /> Which sucks. So no. Not doing that,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:37:05-07:00","id":1306624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306603#post1306603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Ahk I was wrong about when Aura starts, my mistake)<br /> Ok yeah, without between-turn reflexives, Aura becomes ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?<br /> <br /> Though speaking of Dragon Kin Empowerment, that would definitely be one way for a Lore specialist (usually an Air Aspect using Air Charms for an Air Aura) to allow their Resistance specialist ally to actually use RHFD by handing over an Air Aura.<br /> <br /> It would likewise empower a Melee specialist who wants to use Mela\u2019s Forking Tongue at full power, but there aren\u2019t a bunch of other out-of-place Air elemental pinnacle Charms to make me think this is a deliberate trend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:39:20-07:00","id":1306625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306603#post1306603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Ahk I was wrong about when Aura starts, my mistake)<br /> Ok yeah, without between-turn reflexives, Aura becomes ridiculous. Basically if you don\u2019t have everyone take Dragon-kin empowerment, you should ignore any charm that isn\u2019t your aspect.<br /> <br /> Which sucks. So no. Not doing that,.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a pretty big incentive, but I don\u2019t think you should just ignore any charm that isn\u2019t your aspect. At the very least balanced charms are no problem.<br /> <br /> Also you can do stuff without Aura like combo Become the Hammer, Water Dragon Coils, Inescapable Whirlpool Hold, Oaken Thew Exertion, Crushing Avalanche Grasp, Entangling Roots Embrace, and Currents Sweep to Sea. That\u2019s mixing Water, Earth and Wood all together in a big mega combo that doesn\u2019t even touch Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T15:15:59-07:00","id":1306660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306625#post1306625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a pretty big incentive, but I don\u2019t think you should just ignore any charm that isn\u2019t your aspect. At the very least balanced charms are no problem.<br /> <br /> Also you can do stuff without Aura like combo Become the Hammer, Water Dragon Coils, Inescapable Whirlpool Hold, Oaken Thew Exertion, Crushing Avalanche Grasp, Entangling Roots Embrace, and Currents Sweep to Sea. That\u2019s mixing Water, Earth and Wood all together in a big mega combo that doesn\u2019t even touch Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that worth the cost? Blow out all your motes at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T17:31:42-07:00","id":1306686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306660#post1306660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is that worth the cost? Blow out all your motes at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe! You can of course, trim charms to taste. For example if your target isn\u2019t at Short range from you, then you don\u2019t need Currents Sweep to Sea. On the other hand if you have 5/3/5 in your attribute spread and a powerful archer that\u2019s just pelting arrows into your melee combat from short range and causing all kinds of Hell, that combo will grab him by the throat, haul him into melee with the rest of you and keep him there while you drip drain all the initiative out of him. And it works from a position of you yourself having very low initiative, since you\u2019re getting bonus dice and disappearing 6s to the initiative roll.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t say \u201cyes, this is the combo that I will use, my combat strategy is to get this finisher off ASAP and win.\u201d But it\u2019s an option, you could use it along side other options that might include Aura charms. You could even be REALLY nasty and spring that from stealth while you\u2019re under water or in some other kind of environmental effect that you\u2019re immune to. Now all of a sudden you\u2019re making an ambush attack from the river against an enemy, where you snag them, drag them down into it in a single attack, and restrain them while they drown and bleed initiative to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T19:42:11-07:00","id":1306721,"title":"","content":"Having to expend aura so your MA charms don't suck is incredibly silly. I just houserule that once a DB has learned every single charm in an Immaculate Martial Art they ignore the Terrestrial keyword on *all* charms they know from then on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T03:58:36-07:00","id":1306793,"title":"","content":"Considering they'd need to be essence 5 for that, that seems fair. But for most dragon blooded I can see why it's restricted to aura expenditure.<br /> <br /> Martial arts without the terrestrial keyword *need* to be stronger than dragon blooded charms, because they need to be worth buying for other exalted with stronger native charms. If you remove the terrestrial restriction too easily then it becomes pointless for dragon blooded to take anything else.<br /> <br /> And for martial artists it's not like getting into aura is <i>hard</i>. You just need to use your anima power to stunt all the time. Non-immaculate martial arts don't have any affect on aura, so it'll stay up til you need to spend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-22-2019, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:19:10-07:00","id":1306821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306793#post1306793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering they'd need to be essence 5 for that, that seems fair. But for most dragon blooded I can see why it's restricted to aura expenditure.<br /> <br /> Martial arts without the terrestrial keyword *need* to be stronger than dragon blooded charms, because they need to be worth buying for other exalted with stronger native charms. If you remove the terrestrial restriction too easily then it becomes pointless for dragon blooded to take anything else.<br /> <br /> And for martial artists it's not like getting into aura is <i>hard</i>. You just need to use your anima power to stunt all the time. Non-immaculate martial arts don't have any affect on aura, so it'll stay up til you need to spend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be fine if it weren't for Aura duration charms which you basically have to reactivate. Also, CMA in previous editions was always the stronger choice, it just required more effort to learn. Which was why it had higher xp costs. Considering you have to dedicate yourself to MA. And invest more than any other ability, it should have these advantages.<br /> <br /> Though I will say, I'm not fond of how casually Immaculate styles are just a given out in this edition. First edition really stressed how much it took and what kind of dedication it took for Dragon Blooded to master. Now it's kind of just a style specialized for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:32:39-07:00","id":1306822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306793#post1306793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering they'd need to be essence 5 for that, that seems fair. But for most dragon blooded I can see why it's restricted to aura expenditure.<br /> <br /> Martial arts without the terrestrial keyword *need* to be stronger than dragon blooded charms, because they need to be worth buying for other exalted with stronger native charms. If you remove the terrestrial restriction too easily then it becomes pointless for dragon blooded to take anything else.<br /> <br /> And for martial artists it's not like getting into aura is <i>hard</i>. You just need to use your anima power to stunt all the time. Non-immaculate martial arts don't have any affect on aura, so it'll stay up til you need to spend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you even need to stunt? You can\u2019t spend Aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword without having some Immaculate Style Charms up to the form, so you can throw a Charmed Fire Dragon kick out in one turn to tear up the floor with an unlimited Swaying Grass Charm on the next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:35:40-07:00","id":1306824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306821#post1306821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be fine if it weren't for Aura duration charms which you basically have to reactivate. Also, CMA in previous editions was always the stronger choice, it just required more effort to learn. Which was why it had higher xp costs. Considering you have to dedicate yourself to MA. And invest more than any other ability, it should have these advantages.<br /> <br /> Though I will say, I'm not fond of how casually Immaculate styles are just a given out in this edition. First edition really stressed how much it took and what kind of dedication it took for Dragon Blooded to master. Now it's kind of just a style specialized for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one thing I think the Essence scaling for the styles would pretty much limit it. You wouldn't be a master of a Dragon Style until your Essence 5 and thats rare, no supernal here to help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:44:21-07:00","id":1306828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306822#post1306822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you even need to stunt? You can\u2019t spend Aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword without having some Immaculate Style Charms up to the form, so you can throw a Charmed Fire Dragon kick out in one turn to tear up the floor with an unlimited Swaying Grass Charm on the next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't be possible without being a wood aspected dragon blooded who hits bonfire. However, then you'd never go back into your fire aura and fire dragon would essentially be worthless. An immaculate gets extremely punished for attempting to master another style other than his own element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T06:50:35-07:00","id":1306833,"title":"","content":"Er, swaying grass is the capoeira-based martial art from lunars. It's not wood-aspected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T07:14:00-07:00","id":1306840,"title":"","content":"Yeah. An Immaculate Monk is encouraged to learn a single Immaculate Style of their Aspect then learn whatever off Immaculate styles combine with it, because then as long as they use an appropriate charm from their style. They enter the Aura.<br /> <br /> I think Water aspects have it easiest due to Excelleny as I understand it. But almost all of the Immaculate styles have a kinda cheap early charm that's useful for getting the Aura each round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T07:21:51-07:00","id":1306842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306833#post1306833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, swaying grass is the capoeira-based martial art from lunars. It's not wood-aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to be, but not anymore. ONLY the Immaculate Styles are elemental in Third Edition.<br /> <br /> An Earth Aspect can use an Air Dragon Style Charm to get an Air Aura that she then uses to surpass the Terrestrial keyword of a Golden Janissary Charm on the next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T07:32:50-07:00","id":1306847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306842#post1306842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It used to be, but not anymore. ONLY the Immaculate Styles are elemental in Third Edition.<br /> <br /> An Earth Aspect can use an Air Dragon Style Charm to get an Air Aura that she then uses to surpass the Terrestrial keyword of a Golden Janissary Charm on the next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that at bonfire you can't switch into any other aura other than your aspect. I'm not even sure if you can still use one element and stay in aura or if you have to stick to your own element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:57:47-07:00","id":1306902,"title":"","content":"Honestly the Immaculate Dragon Styles are another source of annoyance for me. Yes, they don't have Terrestrial keywords, but they are not very good styles. I'd say almost all of the other styles are stronger, even when limited by Terrestrial keywords. Earth Dragon is the best of the 5, Wood dragon is okay, Water and Air are meh, and Fire sucks ass (not gonna shed a single tear for fire dragons, they already have Melee and Dodge).<br /> <br /> But aside from them not being very good, the very big problem they have is that they are super stingy with their form weapons. Every DB who wants to become serious about MA will feel very pressured to eventually buy his aspect's IMA up to at least the form, but each style has only one weapon + unarmed, which really limits your options.<br /> <br /> Air Dragon has the chakram which no other style uses, so go unarmed or go home.<br /> Earth Dragon has the tetsubo which has the same problem, but at least it allows all types of armor.<br /> Fire Dragon has short swords, which combine with Steel Devil and MAYBE if your ST feels pity for you Single Point.<br /> Wood Dragon has staves, which are shared as form weapons by Golden Janissary, White Reaper and Laughinf Monster. We'll probably see a few more styles using staves in the future, but that's a pretty good spread.<br /> Water Dragon has tiger claws, which work for Tiger, Ebon Shadow, Centipede and Falcon, making it the most flexible atm<br /> <br /> A terrestrial who wants to practice Snake, Crane, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Black Claw, Mantis, White Veil or Swaying Grass Dance is forced to go unarmed-only.<br /> If they want to practice Single Point, Silver-Voiced Nightingale or Righteous Devil then you'll either be forced to stick with Terrestrial keywords or buy 5 dead charms.<br /> <br /> And going unarmed is not a small demerit, its in fact a bigger tradeoff for DBs than for other exalts because it means they can't use artifact weapons, which means they not only do they lose lots of free stats on all withering attacks but also lose out on Resonant Evocations, which is one of the greatest sources of power-parity for DBs.<br /> <br /> This all taken together means DB martial artists are very limited in their choice of styles as well; some styles are only viable with some aspects, and some styles become dramatically worse chioces for DBs as a whole. Also a lot of cool MA weapons like hook-swords, seven-section staves, fans, etc. are not all that useable.<br /> <br /> And that is Bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:02:50-07:00","id":1306903,"title":"","content":"What's you're problem with Fire Dragon? It's seems sufficiently powerful it just lacks defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:12:05-07:00","id":1306908,"title":"","content":"Um aren't style weapons are generally meant to be restricting? Like yeah the Dragon styles have tend to go solo and that is limiting, but all MAs are the same to an extent. So yeah if you want to combo you would have to go at it Unarmed but really I don't see much of a problem with that. though that just be my limited view on it anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-22-2019, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:20:16-07:00","id":1306911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306847#post1306847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that at bonfire you can't switch into any other aura other than your aspect. I'm not even sure if you can still use one element and stay in aura or if you have to stick to your own element.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once you're already at Bonfire, you can use other element-tagged Charms, but you lose your aspect's Aura and you can only get Aura if you use your own Aspect's Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:20:37-07:00","id":1306912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306908#post1306908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um aren't style weapons are generally meant to be restricting? Like yeah the Dragon styles have tend to go solo and that is limiting, but all MAs are the same to an extent. So yeah if you want to combo you would have to go at it Unarmed but really I don't see much of a problem with that. though that just be my limited view on it anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that immaculate styles are okay but they aren't remotely at the level of single point style. You don't even have the option to master them for a long time due to high essence requirements so you have to go into another style to get more martial arts. To have only one style be accessible with form weapons greatly limits them. Unless you have an artifact or native charms that give you that option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:21:51-07:00","id":1306913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306911#post1306911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Once you're already at Bonfire, you can use other element-tagged Charms, but you lose your aspect's Aura and you can only get Aura if you use your own Aspect's Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, yeah you get hosed by trying to break convention. Which honestly feels like a huge unnecessary restriction with aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:36:28-07:00","id":1306918,"title":"","content":"As an adendum to my last post:<br /> <br /> Terrestrial keywords vary greatly in importance, but on some styles they are not so bad. For the type of character who for example is mostly a social guy but picks up some Silver-Voiced Nightingale to be able to contribute to combat encounters while taking advantage of his high social stats, things are fine. What I outlined on my previous post is only REALLY a problem for characters who want to be combat focused and/or want &quot;being a master martial artist&quot; to be an important part of their concept.<br /> <br /> For Serious Martial Artists<sup>TM</sup> Aspect becomes a really important choice:<br /> <br /> Water Aspects are probably still the overall best: MA is an Aspect ability for them, they can enter Water Aura with just the excellency, and Water Dragon has the best weapon compatibility and pretty good armor compatibility. Also worth noting is that they have easy access to Embracing The Violent Flow, the Brawl Water signature charm, which is very strong and compatible with all unarmed martial arts, and could be a solution to a &quot;no artifacts&quot; build.<br /> <br /> Earth Aspects are pretty good too: Earth Dragon is the strongest of the Immaculate Styles and is the only one compatible with all kinds of armor, and they have access to Earth Resistance. They are pretty mush locked to unarmed-only though if they want ot combine any other styles. White Reaper is a good accompaniment . If they do go unarmed, then Crater Making Impact (Earth Brawl signature) can be worth picking up, as can Earth Thrown.<br /> <br /> Fire Aspect is weird: their IMA is the worst by far, BUT Fire Dodge is great and is only really viable for Fire Aspects. So they are a good choice if you want to main a MA that likes to use Evasion mainly (Snake, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Centipede, Swaying Grass Dance and Laughing Monster off the top of my head) or if you want to do Steel Devil specifically. They also have Socialize and Presence as Aspect abilities, so you could pick them to go with social-heavy MA like White Veil, Black Claw and Dreaming Pearl. Good signature picks for them could be Unbinding the Inner Flame or Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, as well as Aura of Invulnerability.<br /> <br /> Wood Aspects are okay: their MA is pretty good an combines well with others, White Reaper specially. Other than that there's not much to say about them. I guess you could combine their Wood Performance charms with Silver-Voiced Nightingale, I have a player in my game doing just that and he's doing okay. They have a scene long Appearance booster in Vivacious Dragon Beauty, so I guess thay would make good Dreaming Pearl Courtesans, or you could go with Snake/White Veil/Centipede if you want to play up the poison aspect.<br /> <br /> Air Aspects are the worst off: light armor + unarmed only, and Air Dragon Style is really not very good. The only really viable option I can think of is taking advantage of Air Stealth and using Air Dragon + Ebon Shadow for an assassin build. Their Brawl signature, Flying Whirlwind Razor, is really really good, but I feel like its wasted on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:44:36-07:00","id":1306923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306908#post1306908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um aren't style weapons are generally meant to be restricting? Like yeah the Dragon styles have tend to go solo and that is limiting, but all MAs are the same to an extent. So yeah if you want to combo you would have to go at it Unarmed but really I don't see much of a problem with that. though that just be my limited view on it anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but going unarmed for a DB means giving up Artifacts and Evocations and that's a huge loss. And there are several MAs that are really friendly weapons-wise: Mantis has 6, Ebon Shadow has 4, Centipede has 5, etc. Aside from the specialized ones like Black Claw or Righteous Devil, all MA so far have at least 2 form weapons and most have at least three.<br /> <br /> There's really no excuse for IMA having only one weapon other than &quot;it was this way in previous editions&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:34:47-07:00","id":1306946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306903#post1306903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's you're problem with Fire Dragon? It's seems sufficiently powerful it just lacks defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy here I go<br /> <br /> Flash Fire Technique is stupid. With this game's math, two rolls is never going to be as good as +5 dice, which means it only ever makes sense to use this on top of a full excellency. BUT you have to pay for the excellency twice, since the charm is pointless if one of the two rolls is significantly smaller than the other. So this charm actually costs you 10m, or 12m with an aplicable specialty, which is unusable with DB Essence pools and the benefir isn't even that good.<br /> <br /> Flame-Flicker Stance is useless without Aura, and even with it is hamstrung by the fact that it counts against charm cap which for DBs is +3 at most. This is without taking into account the fact that everyone and their mother can reroll 1s. Plus this style can only ever use light weapons and Dodge is a Fire Aspect ability, so why the fuck would I want to use Parry?<br /> <br /> The form sucks and I hate it. The first part can be negated by anyone who is not a DB and many who are, and the second will barely ever come into play. And that's it? That's all it does? What a joke.<br /> <br /> Essence-Igniting Nerve Strike is useless without Aura (seeing a pattern yet?) and you have to roll at least 14 dice of withering damage (very very hard when all you have are light weapons and no withering damage boosters) for the opponent to lose the same motes on average than what you spent on this charm without counting the willpower. If by some miracle you get the Crash you deal what? 2 dice of damage? that's less than 1 health level on average. And this is only at Essence 3 against a lower initiative opponent.<br /> <br /> Overwhelming Fire Majesty Stance is suicidal without Aura, and merely very expensive with Aura. As a defense its half as efficient as the excellency, so its only really useful against lots of attacks or as a cap breaker. EXCEPT, and opponent can spend 1w and ignore it for the rest of the fight. Fucking what? and what's with the Charisma scaling? This charm is a higher-requirement higher-cost copy of Fearsome Dragon Presence.<br /> <br /> Breath of the Fire Dragon is worse than its Air, Earth and Water counterparts and vastly inferior to the visually-identical cousin Terrifying Roar of the Fire Dragon. At Essence 4.<br /> <br /> Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon is laughably weak for an Essence 5 capstone. It can snowball if you can somehow increase the damage a couple of times but what kills it is that it in order to use it you have to be in the aforementioned shitty ass form.<br /> <br /> Searing Edge Attack, Perfect Blazing Blow and Fiery Blade Attack are legitimately good, but none of them are amazing, nor are they very sinergistic, and they can't compensate for the deluge of shit that the rest of the style is.<br /> <br /> God I apologize for my tone here but I had forgotten just how bitter I am about this style and IMA as a whole. Fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:41:17-07:00","id":1306947,"title":"","content":"Eh. I have no problem with that. I haven't played as a db so it's useful to see the faults. I don't disagree with most of it. And I was actually going to get into other styles soon. Though I do think fire majesty is actually pretty useful for the build i'm going for where i constantly use charms that require willpower to combat against.<br /> <br /> Edit- i will say that in this edition the immaculate styles just feel like dragon blooded level charms, barring a few exceptions, rather than martial art level charms. <br /> <br /> Despite being E5, i can't see anyone other than dragon blooded picking them up. Because they really don't hit the level that they need to compared to other styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-22-2019, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:14:18-07:00","id":1306955,"title":"","content":"...are any of you guys getting into combats against things that aren\u2019t Celestial exalts...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:28:00-07:00","id":1306960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306955#post1306955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...are any of you guys getting into combats against things that aren\u2019t Celestial exalts...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to how in previous editions the Immaculate styles were clearly above what dragon blooded could do. In this edition, I'm looking at other combat styles and it's really not much difference. There are a few exceptions. However, comparing fire to snake in this edition and snake is honestly better even with the terrestrial kneecaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:28:05-07:00","id":1306961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306955#post1306955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...are any of you guys getting into combats against things that aren\u2019t Celestial exalts...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of Course, I'm also fightning their conspicuously capable hordes of brainwashed peasants.<br /> On a more serious note, I do expect my Immaculate Shikari to be somewhat competent at hunting Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:37:17-07:00","id":1306964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306847#post1306847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that at bonfire you can't switch into any other aura other than your aspect. I'm not even sure if you can still use one element and stay in aura or if you have to stick to your own element.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a problem if you learned the Form Charm of the Immaculate Style of your Aspect's element, which almost every Terrestrial would do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:41:02-07:00","id":1306966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306964#post1306964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't a problem if you learned the Form Charm of the Immaculate Style of your Aspect's element, which almost every Terrestrial would do.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? That only removes terrestrial for one turn and if you have defenses in dodge or resistance you are giving up Aura long defensive charms that cost willpower to activate in order to do it. In addition, if you have those aura charms off-aspect you'll never be able to turn them back on until you manage your anima flux. The only way to realistically do this is with specific charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-22-2019, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:41:02-07:00","id":1306967,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:16:19-07:00","id":1306976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306961#post1306961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of Course, I'm also fightning their conspicuously capable hordes of brainwashed peasants..</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306961#post1306961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, I do expect my Immaculate Shikari to be somewhat competent at hunting Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, of course, but even career Shikari are going to fight things that aren\u2019t Celestials more often than they battle Solar/Lunar anathema. Even then a Fire Dragon master is going to totally roll a bespectacled little bureaucracy Supernal or something. If you\u2019re crossing blades with a manticore or a buck-ogre you\u2019re golden. Or some house Sesus dog that thinks he can just eavesdrop on your private conversations with grandmother.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re only running into serious problems of certain charms being ineffective if you\u2019re facing a melee Supernal or something, and that\u2019s supposed to feel like a suicide mission. That\u2019s why they\u2019re sending 5 of you, your demon bodyguards, your network of spies and a cadre of Immaculate monks as backup, who are not even going to rush in there before laying a complex multi-stage trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:26:34-07:00","id":1306979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306960#post1306960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm referring to how in previous editions the Immaculate styles were clearly above what dragon blooded could do. In this edition, I'm looking at other combat styles and it's really not much difference. There are a few exceptions. However, comparing fire to snake in this edition and snake is honestly better even with the terrestrial kneecaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s a problem. Also Single Point is a pretty serious problem, I don\u2019t think any future MA will ever be published and considered decent next to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:28:10-07:00","id":1306980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306966#post1306966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? That only removes terrestrial for one turn and if you have defenses in dodge or resistance you are giving up Aura long defensive charms that cost willpower to activate in order to do it. In addition, if you have those aura charms off-aspect you'll never be able to turn them back on until you manage your anima flux. The only way to realistically do this is with specific charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we weren't talking about Dodge or Resistance. We were talking about Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:01:50-07:00","id":1306991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306979#post1306979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that\u2019s a problem. Also Single Point is a pretty serious problem, I don\u2019t think any future MA will ever be published and considered decent next to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Single Point is actually not that great for a terrestrial. Because of the limitations of the Aura system, the terrestrial keyword makes it worse than other styles. However, looking at snake, mantis, crane. All the base styles still do quite more than any of the immaculate charms. Apart from some effects which are unique, like water has a true perfect and the ability to end charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:02:40-07:00","id":1306992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306980#post1306980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we weren't talking about Dodge or Resistance. We were talking about Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can't talk about Martial arts without talking about those skills because unlike melee, Martial arts doesn't have a full set of defensive abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:14:01-07:00","id":1306998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306992#post1306992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can't talk about Martial arts without talking about those skills because unlike melee, Martial arts doesn't have a full set of defensive abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you stepped into a conversation I was having with someone else about using multiple Martial Arts together in order to generate and spend Auras to surpass the Terrestrial keyword. Not about strategies that relied on multiple Abilities.<br /> <br /> You may be right, but you can't just move the goalposts without being explicit and open that you are doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:14:53-07:00","id":1306999,"title":"","content":"Fire Dragon is pretty clearly at its most effective when fighting rogue spirits and gods, which don\u2019t have any printed charms for negating onslaught or rerolling 1s. It\u2019s also way more effective used in combination with other Shikari or just with any kind of backup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:19:08-07:00","id":1307002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306998#post1306998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you stepped into a conversation I was having with someone else about using multiple Martial Arts together in order to generate and spend Auras to surpass the Terrestrial keyword. Not about strategies that relied on multiple Abilities.<br /> <br /> You may be right, but you can't just move the goalposts without being explicit and open that you are doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I see. I suppose if you were just generating and spending Auras that wouldn't be hard that honestly doesn't feel efficient especially when most terrestrial limitations are kind of minor. Most of them are &quot;This expensive charm is now once per scene&quot;. There are some major exceptions. Like Shining point is garbage for Dragon blooded because all the terrestrial limitations and the fact that the form charm is limited. There's no way expend enough auras to negate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:28:58-07:00","id":1307007,"title":"","content":"Shining point's issue is that the mastery effect is busted to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:33:03-07:00","id":1307009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307007#post1307007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shining point's issue is that the mastery effect is busted to hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That too but for dragon blooded that terrestrial effect is also an issue. Like shining point in the hands of a solar a lunar and a dragon blooded are completely because the terrestrial effects aren't insignificant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:39:07-07:00","id":1307015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306991#post1306991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Single Point is actually not that great for a terrestrial. Because of the limitations of the Aura system, the terrestrial keyword makes it worse than other styles. However, looking at snake, mantis, crane. All the base styles still do quite more than any of the immaculate charms. Apart from some effects which are unique, like water has a true perfect and the ability to end charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think saying that they do a lot more than the Immaculate styles is a bit far. The Immaculate styles don\u2019t make you as powerful as a Solar or anything because the entire setting makes absolutely no sense if they did that, but you\u2019ve got things like Hurricane Combat Method or Weapon Breaking Defense that both let you take additional reflexive attack actions, and the latter even lets you grab hold of an enemy\u2019s daiklave and snap it in half. <br /> <br /> Or just crazy/cool stuff like combining Tornado Offence Technique with Avenging Wind Strike, especially if you\u2019re launching it while hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:47:13-07:00","id":1307017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307015#post1307015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think saying that they do a lot more than the Immaculate styles is a bit far. The Immaculate styles don\u2019t make you as powerful as a Solar or anything because the entire setting makes absolutely no sense if they did that, but you\u2019ve got things like Hurricane Combat Method or Weapon Breaking Defense that both let you take additional reflexive attack actions, and the latter even lets you grab hold of an enemy\u2019s daiklave and snap it in half.<br /> <br /> Or just crazy/cool stuff like combining Tornado Offence Technique with Avenging Wind Strike, especially if you\u2019re launching it while hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the immaculate styles are supposed to be as strong as a style is before the mastery keyword but most of the styles feel like dragon blooded charms rather than something closer to non-mastery core styles.<br /> <br /> They were supposed to be stronger than baseline dragon blooded charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:51:59-07:00","id":1307019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1306999#post1306999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire Dragon is pretty clearly at its most effective when fighting rogue spirits and gods, which don\u2019t have any printed charms for negating onslaught or rerolling 1s. It\u2019s also way more effective used in combination with other Shikari or just with any kind of backup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be wrong about this but I think nobody except Solars and Lunars have charms for rerolling 1s. I think <br /> <br /> I can understand some of the frustration, I think, because you look at all the aura effects and stuff from different elements, and just like the Solar charmset you start going \u201cwow, if I combo this with this with this I could kill Alhat in one shot before he even ACTS!\u201d But then you realize you can\u2019t actually do that and it sucks, because Solars and Lunars get to combine everything all day and terrestrials don\u2019t. You\u2019re not really supposed to be able to do that as a DB though. If you feel like facing off against a very combat focused Dawn is a losing proposition, that\u2019s good, that\u2019s what it\u2019s supposed to be. A super powerful DB is supposed to be more a match for like a fairfolk Carapgract, and they absolutely are.<br /> <br /> The problem in 2e was that you could have an elite death squad of 5 Immaculate grandmasters and one Solar would eat them for breakfast with no contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:02:11-07:00","id":1307022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307019#post1307019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand some of the frustration, I think, because you look at all the aura effects and stuff from different elements, and just like the Solar charmset you start going \u201cwow, if I combo this with this with this I could kill Alhat in one shot before he even ACTS!\u201d But then you realize you can\u2019t actually do that and it sucks, because Solars and Lunars get to combine everything all day and terrestrials don\u2019t. You\u2019re not really supposed to be able to do that as a DB though. If you feel like facing off against a very combat focused Dawn is a losing proposition, that\u2019s good, that\u2019s what it\u2019s supposed to be. A super powerful DB is supposed to be more a match for like a fairfolk Carapgract, and they absolutely are..</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is you have to buy dead charms and several combinations of abilities are completely barred off because they only work with with specific elements. It's not just about combining charms but about the fact that that you get punished for not combining the right ones. <br /> <br /> The deal with immaculate styles is a different issue where these styles are supposed to be strong as regular martial arts but it feels like they lose out versus mundane versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:14:35-07:00","id":1307029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307017#post1307017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the immaculate styles are supposed to be as strong as a style is before the mastery keyword but most of the styles feel like dragon blooded charms rather than something closer to non-mastery core styles.<br /> <br /> They were supposed to be stronger than baseline dragon blooded charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think they\u2019re supposed to be quite that powerful. If they were as powerful as you can get without provoking Mastery then they\u2019d be as powerful as the best Lunar charms, which can\u2019t happen.<br /> <br /> They ARE some of the most powerful charms available to Dragonblooded though, barring dubiously balances corebook styles and evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:17:51-07:00","id":1307030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307029#post1307029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think they\u2019re supposed to be quite that powerful. If they were as powerful as you can get without provoking Mastery then they\u2019d be as powerful as the best Lunar charms, which can\u2019t happen.<br /> <br /> They ARE some of the most powerful charms available to Dragonblooded though, barring dubiously balances corebook styles and evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they wouldn't because lunars get to combine with native charms. The styles are treated as if they are strong as other styles in the core but the problem is they just aren't. Outside of getting a form charm, for aura use the styles aren't as good as they used to be. Which is ironic.<br /> <br /> Also, they aren't some of the most powerful charms available to the dragon-blooded because they can still use other styles and then aura away the problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:23:40-07:00","id":1307033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307022#post1307022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is you have to buy dead charms and several combinations of abilities are completely barred off because they only work with with specific elements. It's not just about combining charms but about the fact that that you get punished for not combining the right ones. <br /> <br /> The deal with immaculate styles is a different issue where these styles are supposed to be strong as regular martial arts but it feels like they lose out versus mundane versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead charms I get, but the combining specific charms I don\u2019t really. You are supposed to be less flexible but more powerful in certain ways while sticking to one element. If you want you can be a wood aspect who uses a bunch of fire charms and mixes them with water and earth and whatever, but you\u2019re going to have a hard time using Heartbeats Before Death, which is a bloody awesome DB charm.<br /> <br /> Buuut if you want to use Heartbeats Before Death you need to lay off on the Hopping Firecracker Evasion. Or possibly do some convoluted thing where you use Firecracker Evasion to go bonfire into your wood aura or something. The two don\u2019t work well together because mixing elements and leaning hard into one element are supposed to be relatively balanced against one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:27:23-07:00","id":1307036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307033#post1307033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dead charms I get, but the combining specific charms I don\u2019t really. You are supposed to be less flexible but more powerful in certain ways while sticking to one element. If you want you can be a wood aspect who uses a bunch of fire charms and mixes them with water and earth and whatever, but you\u2019re going to have a hard time using Heartbeats Before Death, which is a bloody awesome DB charm.<br /> <br /> Buuut if you want to use Heartbeats Before Death you need to lay off on the Hopping Firecracker Evasion. Or possibly do some convoluted thing where you use Firecracker Evasion to go bonfire into your wood aura or something. The two don\u2019t work well together because mixing elements and leaning hard into one element are supposed to be relatively balanced against one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem. Why is it fair for the ability that has two defensive techniques out of three to have all the same element. Fire is clearly at an unfair advantage because Wood has no real way to go into dodge or resistance or melee. These are restrictions upon restrictions. That only way it'd work in an ideal world is one where the dragon blooded book charmset is 4x as large as it is to accommodate every element equally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-22-2019, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:37:50-07:00","id":1307044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307036#post1307036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the problem. Why is it fair for the ability that has two defensive techniques out of three to have all the same element. Fire is clearly at an unfair advantage because Wood has no real way to go into dodge or resistance or melee. These are restrictions upon restrictions. That only work in an ideal world where the dragon blooded book charmset is 4x as large as it is to accommodate every element equally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because fire doesn\u2019t have the ability to go into thrown or archery or resistance. If you lean really hard into wood you can cherry pick a few things from dodge and go hard into archery so you can sit at short range, turn your weapon into heavy cover and plunk away with your bow. Or go hard into Ride too and ride around disengaging and then reflexively aiming with Elusive Skirmisher. Fire could go hard into dodge, but if they do then their ability to use archery and/or ride is super limited.<br /> <br /> Each element can\u2019t do every ability equally, but they can each do their own thing better than any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:46:29-07:00","id":1307049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307044#post1307044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because fire doesn\u2019t have the ability to go into thrown or archery or resistance. If you lean really hard into wood you can cherry pick a few things from dodge and go hard into archery so you can sit at short range, turn your weapon into heavy cover and plunk away with your bow. Or go hard into Ride too and ride around disengaging and then reflexively aiming with Elusive Skirmisher. Fire could go hard into dodge, but if they do then their ability to use archery and/or ride is super limited.<br /> <br /> Each element can\u2019t do every ability equally, but they can each do their own thing better than any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this isn't good because basically you're telling dragon blooded that it's okay to get screwed for not being the right element. This not good design when you have 3 elements struggling to get defensive charms while 2 others hog them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:50:11-07:00","id":1307050,"title":"","content":"Being completely honest, these are several interlocked issues, not just one. Aura, as an idea, is pretty awesome; you give up flexibility in order to gain power, or you lose power and gain in flexibility.<br /> <br /> The issue then comes around when the DB Charmset makes about no sense in where it puts elemental tags. The Entombed Mind tree, which has nothing to do with combat and is in fact actively counter to combat, and which consists of three Earth Charms? It comes after the DB Fire version of Poised Lion Attitude, Eternally Argumentative Flame. The Melee capstones? Water, Air, literally anything but fire. Besides having a Wood Charm in between two Fire Charms and other similar shenanigans.<br /> <br /> But then you go &quot;Oh that just means I get more chances to juggle Auras around and enter different ones!&quot; Wrong. With how absurdly costly the DB Charms are as a whole, you're hitting bonfire by your first or second turn, if not straight out of Join Battle, which means no Aura juggling for you. Which is the third component of this problem. The fourth is that many Charms are next to useless without Aura, and that other many ones would seem useless without each other but they're different elements. These issues sort of soften themselves out by Essence 3+ since you're getting to the actually decent part of the Charmset, but by then you're picking Signatures, many of which have the Aura keyword, and many of which do not support the Aura it requires at all (Water Melee Signature). And THEN there's the part where defensive Charms only disrupt and end and prevent your Aura, but do not create it, which is one of the dumbest parts of it. <br /> <br /> All in all, with how the DB set is, Aura translates to the feeling of getting choked out of fun and options the moment you try to use your powers, despite Aura itself being fine in a vacuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:51:19-07:00","id":1307052,"title":"","content":"I still think we should have moved Brawl/MA to Earth, War to Fire, and Dodge to Water to even out the mechanics a bit more. Sticking Melee and Dodge in the same aspect was a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:06:50-07:00","id":1307057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307052#post1307052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think we should have moved Brawl/MA to Earth, War to Fire, and Dodge to Water to even out the mechanics a bit more. Sticking Melee and Dodge in the same aspect was a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could have been fine if defense charms were mostly balanced and each element had an individual pinnacle. Balance was not something that was used as often as it should have been.<br /> <br /> But as is, it's kind of a mess of elements that kind of detracts from the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-22-2019, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:39:00-07:00","id":1307072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307049#post1307049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except this isn't good because basically you're telling dragon blooded that it's okay to get screwed for not being the right element. This not good design when you have 3 elements struggling to get defensive charms while 2 others hog them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They kind of do. Before Essence 4 in dodge the only defensive charm Fire gets that isn't also balanced is Flickering Candle, which isn't bad but the excellency lets you ignore environmental penalties anyway. Technically Ember Emits Smoke also raises evasion but it's more expensive than the excellency so you're really just paying for the counterattack. Once you get to Essence 3 fire's sig is another counter attack, where Woods actually gives you better defence and Water lets you cancel damage. Air gets Elusive Crosswind and fire gets Bonfire Shadow Evasion for actual defence boosts, so that's pretty even. Bonfire Shadow is actually probably the worst one until you get Coiling Dragon at essence 4, at which point I'd say Fire does pull ahead slightly, and then the essence 5 charm is omni-elemental and even retroactively reassigns elements to prior charms. What Fire gets by going hard into dodge isn't defence as much as it is Evasion based counterattacks and like pseudo disengage rushes and stuff.<br /> <br /> For melee the only dedicated defensive charms in the tree is balanced in FBI and Water in graceful flowing defense, even the clash accuracy booster which can be kind of defensive/offensive is balanced. Then we get to the signatures and air gets mobility, earth gets debilitating effects, Fire and water get straight damage, and wood is left with the only one that actually boosts defensive capabilities. Then as we move through Essence 3 wood again is the only one with a defense boost, and it's probably the best in the tree. The closest Fire has is Portenteous Comet Deflection, which lets them try and reflexively clash with a decisive, or Cloud Riot, which is also water and probably better for keeping yourself safe since it's a withering clash. Water also gets another kind of defensive charm at the pinnacle. What Fire gets by being so melee focused is way more damage and defend other charms and stuff.<br /> <br /> Okay, now resistance. ISoS is balanced, then the next two charms are water and wood, and the wood one is actually a stealth Evasion charm anyway because it lowers mobility penalties from armour. Unfeeling Earth is a good charm for Earth aspects who have a lot of ox bodies, eventually if they can stay in aura they just done give a fuck about wounds. For the signatures air and earth are both good, water and wood are decent, but are both really better suited to be used out of combat, and fire actually makes you less durable. Earth Bears Witness is also pretty good for Earth, Water and Wood, immovable mountain technique for Earth is very situational...and then we get into the complete assness that is late DB resistance with two good defensive Water AURA charms that lead into a defensive Air AURA charm. That sucks monkey totem Lunar balls. What earth gets out of resistance more than defense is ignoring food/water/sleep etc. As well as some decent protection charms.<br /> <br /> Then we have even more context too, because thrown and archery and all sorts of other trees have charms that can help defend as well, AND we have the anima powers. Air gets ranged defense Earth gets soak, hardness, and penalty ignoring, Fire gets ...kind of a shitty flame defense, water gets a lot of mobility stuff, and wood gets to ignore penalties to evasion and resist poison.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if your concern is that you hate that Fire gets all the charms to avoid getting hit, and Earth gets all the charms to tank damage, that really isn't the case. On the other hand if you really didn't like how much Fire gets to explosively counterattack with dodge, or defend other a ton, or that the last three charms in resistance have stupid stupid requirements, that's totally valid in my opinion. I don't agree with the former points because I think it's cool that Fire gets to do that as a really unique thing, but I can understand that you might wish you could do that while being hard into Water.<br /> <br /> I also hope that my really long answer isn't coming off as aggressive, it's just really hard to explain in so few words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-22-2019, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:48:33-07:00","id":1307074,"title":"","content":"Oh also defensive charms not creating your aura is really dumb, and I can't believe that was intentional design. Not being able to get into Water Aura using Graceful Flowing Defense and the excellency is no good and I'm going to forget that I heard it was confirmed as working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:52:54-07:00","id":1307075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307002#post1307002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. I see. I suppose if you were just generating and spending Auras that wouldn't be hard that honestly doesn't feel efficient especially when most terrestrial limitations are kind of minor. Most of them are &quot;This expensive charm is now once per scene&quot;. There are some major exceptions. Like Shining point is garbage for Dragon blooded because all the terrestrial limitations and the fact that the form charm is limited. There's no way expend enough auras to negate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't truly relevant to the narrow subject I was covering, though it definitely sounds like an important area to research to determine whether or not spending Auras on the Terrestrial keyword is worth the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:55:09-07:00","id":1307078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307074#post1307074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh also defensive charms not creating your aura is really dumb, and I can't believe that was intentional design. Not being able to get into Water Aura using Graceful Flowing Defense and the excellency is no good and I'm going to forget that I heard it was confirmed as working as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what would be the new timing?<br /> <br /> Currently, all Charms you use on your turn matter, as the Aura only ignites after your turn ends. How does the timing work for Charms you use outside of your turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:59:32-07:00","id":1307080,"title":"","content":"Oh, also I'm not sure if it's good design to have Water aura so easily attainable for a martial artist in the form of the excellency, because then a Water dragon can become really damn close to just being a celestial martial artist by shedding aura every turn and getting it right back. With how powerful the corebook styles can be that might imbalance things a bit toward water. The saving grace there being that most people who play exalted seem to care about character integrity and cohesion.<br /> <br /> We'd have a lot more sorcerers otherwise, lol. Wood Dragon Claw and Invulnerable Skin of Bronze for everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T19:20:26-07:00","id":1307099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307072#post1307072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So if your concern is that you hate that Fire gets all the charms to avoid getting hit, and Earth gets all the charms to tank damage, that really isn't the case. On the other hand if you really didn't like how much Fire gets to explosively counterattack with dodge, or defend other a ton, or that the last three charms in resistance have stupid stupid requirements, that's totally valid in my opinion. I don't agree with the former points because I think it's cool that Fire gets to do that as a really unique thing, but I can understand that you might wish you could do that while being hard into Water.<br /> <br /> I also hope that my really long answer isn't coming off as aggressive, it's just really hard to explain in so few words.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I'm going to be honest. I understand what you are saying. I just don't agree because it's not just about being cool it's about how limiting it is. Air has to buy in like 5 charms to get that one dodge charm that's only useful against arrows. What if they get rushed by an opponent? What if it's a a close ranged attack coming from medium range like the water brawl lets you do. Then an air stylist spent a shitload of waste xp on a move he's not going to be able to use. He loses air effects from turning off aura by using his fire charms. He doesn't gain fire aura and so he has borderline useless charms. He probably also has the air signature but that's once per scene. That's not going to save him at all. <br /> <br /> The dragon blooded are already weak. Their charms are already weak with and without aura and at a level that is definitively under both solars and lunars. It's really not fair that they have to be restricted by aura because it does nothing but hinder character concepts and Dragon blooded more than their charmset already does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-22-2019, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T19:28:38-07:00","id":1307104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307075#post1307075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't truly relevant to the narrow subject I was covering, though it definitely sounds like an important area to research to determine whether or not spending Auras on the Terrestrial keyword is worth the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>That answer is honestly a binary question and not all to hard to answer. How many aura based charms does their fighting style use? If these charms are defensive would not having them be the difference between life and death.<br /> <br /> Personally, if aura duration charms were actually scenelong and the charms effects were suppressed when aura was off. I'd be a lot more forgiving towards the idea. But as it is if you have aura based defensive charms those turn off and most of them have expensive mote and willpower requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T20:01:07-07:00","id":1307116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307099#post1307099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air has to buy in like 5 charms to get that one dodge charm that's only useful against arrows. What if they get rushed by an opponent? What if it's a a close ranged attack coming from medium range like the water brawl lets you do. Then an air stylist spent a shitload of waste xp on a move he's not going to be able to use. He loses air effects from turning off aura by using his fire charms. He doesn't gain fire aura and so he has borderline useless charms. He probably also has the air signature but that's once per scene. That's not going to save him at all.<br /> <br /> The dragon blooded are already weak. Their charms are already weak with and without aura and at a level that is definitively under both solars and lunars. It's really not fair that they have to be restricted by aura because it does nothing but hinder character concepts and Dragon blooded more than their charmset already does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Numbers, numbers, numbers.<br /> <br /> A circle of Dragon-Blooded is more likely to fight one Celestial at a time than multiple ones, and even Celestial combat monsters struggle to attack multiple targets every single round.<br /> <br /> So if you have one of your sworn kin as the designated tank, he can invest all in defense Charms that don't threaten his Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T23:26:07-07:00","id":1307156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307078#post1307078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what would be the new timing?<br /> <br /> Currently, all Charms you use on your turn matter, as the Aura only ignites after your turn ends. How does the timing work for Charms you use outside of your turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably why earlier on I randomly assumed that aura started at the beginning of your Next turn. Having already assumed defensive charms were applicable, I filled in that blank.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily a good way to do it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T06:49:52-07:00","id":1307207,"title":"","content":"There would be no new timing. Aura still ignites at the end of your turn, but then once your tick ends, all Charms you use from that point until the end of your next turn count towards your next Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T07:39:07-07:00","id":1307212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307207#post1307207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would be no new timing. Aura still ignites at the end of your turn, but then once your tick ends, all Charms you use from that point until the end of your next turn count towards your next Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I used Stoking Bonfire Style on my first turn, then Flowing Water Defense outside of my turn, then Stoking Bonfire Style on my second turn, I would:<br /> <br /> Gain a Fire Aura at the end of my first turn, lose it outside of my turn, and then gain a Water Aura at the end of my second turn because SBS's Balance keyword makes it subordinate to the Water element of Flowing Water Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T08:44:33-07:00","id":1307227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307099#post1307099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I'm going to be honest. I understand what you are saying. I just don't agree because it's not just about being cool it's about how limiting it is. Air has to buy in like 5 charms to get that one dodge charm that's only useful against arrows. What if they get rushed by an opponent? What if it's a a close ranged attack coming from medium range like the water brawl lets you do. Then an air stylist spent a shitload of waste xp on a move he's not going to be able to use. He loses air effects from turning off aura by using his fire charms. He doesn't gain fire aura and so he has borderline useless charms. He probably also has the air signature but that's once per scene. That's not going to save him at all.<br /> <br /> The dragon blooded are already weak. Their charms are already weak with and without aura and at a level that is definitively under both solars and lunars. It's really not fair that they have to be restricted by aura because it does nothing but hinder character concepts and Dragon blooded more than their charmset already does.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might also be good to think less about comparing Dragonblooded directly to Solars and Lunars, which in the setting are almost the only two things stronger than they are. Other than that it's only the absolute strongest spirits like Octavian that can compete. Garda Birds, Greenmaws, Tyrant Lizards, even a Nephwrack can't beat a combat focused Dragonblooded, and apart from the Deathlords themselves Nephwracks are the most powerful ghosts in the Underworld. That's not even considering any of their teamwork effects either.<br /> <br /> There are some awkward/bad charm placements though. One or two non-balnced charms that are of a different aspect as prerequisites are okay, but something like Arrow Rain Tempest is probably going too far. I really don't know what the thought process there was you'll be able to use the earlier aura charms if you want to...somehow...? Like being in Wood Aura to use Swallows Defend the Nest is not hard for a Water Aspect to do...?<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think is that if you're using an artifact weapon and/or armor, you probably don't don't need to be burning a full excellency into every attack/defense and can maybe control your bonfire anima enough to reasonably use other auras. Like if you're attacking a Greenmaw or a Bloodape or something your 18 dice attack should just hit their defense of 4-5, and you toss on maybe one mote of Brawl excellency to get the rerolling 6s and another 3m for Stone Fist Strike or something. You get back 5 motes at the start of every turn, so it's possible if you want to spend 10 motes a round to go 3 rounds before touching your peripheral.<br /> <br /> You could also maybe ration your peripheral too once you get to it, if you spend 9 or fewer peripheral motes in an action you'll only go up by one level of anima each time, so you might get 2 or 3 turns out of that, and most combats in my experience don't last longer than 3 turns anyway.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea how viable that tactic is, at all. I've only ever seen Solars act like that before, what with the whole Anathema thing, and they were even more restricted because they had to spend less than 4 motes an action once the personal ran out. This definitely merits some testing in the Arena. Against things that aren't Solar Exalts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307212#post1307212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I used Stoking Bonfire Style on my first turn, then Flowing Water Defense outside of my turn, then Stoking Bonfire Style on my second turn, I would:<br /> <br /> Gain a Fire Aura at the end of my first turn, lose it outside of my turn, and then gain a Water Aura at the end of my second turn because SBS's Balance keyword makes it subordinate to the Water element of Flowing Water Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think that's what I'll be going with personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T09:32:28-07:00","id":1307234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307227#post1307227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might also be good to think less about comparing Dragonblooded directly to Solars and Lunars, which in the setting are almost the only two things stronger than they are. Other than that it's only the absolute strongest spirits like Octavian that can compete. Garda Birds, Greenmaws, Tyrant Lizards, even a Nephwrack can't beat a combat focused Dragonblooded, and apart from the Deathlords themselves Nephwracks are the most powerful ghosts in the Underworld. That's not even considering any of their teamwork effects either.<br /> <br /> There are some awkward/bad charm placements though. One or two non-balnced charms that are of a different aspect as prerequisites are okay, but something like Arrow Rain Tempest is probably going too far. I really don't know what the thought process there was you'll be able to use the earlier aura charms if you want to...somehow...? Like being in Wood Aura to use Swallows Defend the Nest is not hard for a Water Aspect to do...?<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think is that if you're using an artifact weapon and/or armor, you probably don't don't need to be burning a full excellency into every attack/defense and can maybe control your bonfire anima enough to reasonably use other auras. Like if you're attacking a Greenmaw or a Bloodape or something your 18 dice attack should just hit their defense of 4-5, and you toss on maybe one mote of Brawl excellency to get the rerolling 6s and another 3m for Stone Fist Strike or something. You get back 5 motes at the start of every turn, so it's possible if you want to spend 10 motes a round to go 3 rounds before touching your peripheral.<br /> <br /> You could also maybe ration your peripheral too once you get to it, if you spend 9 or fewer peripheral motes in an action you'll only go up by one level of anima each time, so you might get 2 or 3 turns out of that, and most combats in my experience don't last longer than 3 turns anyway.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea how viable that tactic is, at all. I've only ever seen Solars act like that before, what with the whole Anathema thing, and they were even more restricted because they had to spend less than 4 motes an action once the personal ran out. This definitely merits some testing in the Arena. Against things that aren't Solar Exalts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah I think that's what I'll be going with personally.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do remember that Solars and Lunars are consistent enemies of the Dragon-Blooded due to them being Anathema and all. They can cut through your armies, ignore a lot of the teamwork involved through onslaught negation, multi-attack, and many many other things. Comparing DB Charms to Solar and Lunar Charms is of course a futile effort, DB ones will almost always be weaker, but comparing their fighting prowess is important when determining how plausible these Wyld Hunts are. Also, DBs are not the strongest after Solars and Lunars, and are in fact explicitly the weakest of all the Exalted, which means weaker than 9 types of demigod (12 if you use the optional ones), and were described in the IMA section as requiring said martial arts in order to be able to deal with unruly spirits that otherwise overpowered most of them. Fairly certain that spirits like Nephwracks, and animals like Tyrant Lizards, can absolutely obliterate even combat focused DBs if on their own, and really hurt them even in groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T10:12:01-07:00","id":1307243,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure, like there's not disputing DBs are the weakest, but other then Exalts DBs do seem pretty strong to the others, Dr Love Monkey makes a point since its totally viable for DBs to solo those types of enemies, at least when their materialized, otherwise they need to dip into Occult. When it comes down to Wyld Hunts, both Lunars and Solars can deal against groups and negate the benefits as you said, but that doesn't stop the advantages that DBs have from their numbers even if you can deal with the worse. This also brings into question the level of combat investment Solar and Lunars typically get, outside of their combat Castes Full Moons and Dawns which you are the ones who can do the stuff your describing. For the rest the level of investment varies. Its much easier to find a group of middle combat invested DBs then it is so with a Solar Circle(Lunar Circle it be a little more harder, since how easy it is to dip into Attributes). Not to say other Castes can't be strong and their all weak, Nights are the greatest assassins and Zeniths are tough with Resistance and Athletics not to mention they can quickly create armies if they have to and even without any of that just having any of the Solar workhorse charms would be fine to make them powerful foes, but compared to the combat monsters that are Dawns and Full Moons they are more doable for a Wyld Hunt to organize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-23-2019, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T10:41:17-07:00","id":1307249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307234#post1307234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do remember that Solars and Lunars are consistent enemies of the Dragon-Blooded due to them being Anathema and all. They can cut through your armies, ignore a lot of the teamwork involved through onslaught negation, multi-attack, and many many other things. Comparing DB Charms to Solar and Lunar Charms is of course a futile effort, DB ones will almost always be weaker, but comparing their fighting prowess is important when determining how plausible these Wyld Hunts are. Also, DBs are not the strongest after Solars and Lunars, and are in fact explicitly the weakest of all the Exalted, which means weaker than 9 types of demigod (12 if you use the optional ones), and were described in the IMA section as requiring said martial arts in order to be able to deal with unruly spirits that otherwise overpowered most of them. Fairly certain that spirits like Nephwracks, and animals like Tyrant Lizards, can absolutely obliterate even combat focused DBs if on their own, and really hurt them even in groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, fair, DBs are also weaker than Sidereals and Abyssals and the like, but the most common exalt type they face in combat by far is other DBs. The Immaculate order spends way more time putting sandal to god-face than it does battling Lunar anathema out on the boarders of the Empire, and more time exorcising ghosts and crushing cults for that matter. DB vs Solar combat is like, the culmination of an epic story arc that's full of fighting everything that isn't a Solar. It's like the DB version of a Solar campaign that ends with you squaring off against Ligier or something.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of required by the way the setting works, the Realm and Lookshy call a time-out when anathema are spotted nearby to go deal with them together. They send entire armies with dozens, and sometimes even hundreds, of terrestrial exalts. Battling a Solar isn't, or shouldn't be, the norm for your DB campaigns. Unless you got a lot of buy-in from your players as like &quot;This is going to be a highlights reel of the ends of Wyld Hunts.&quot; or maybe if your ST is just a dick.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also Tyrant Lizards and Nephwracks get riggity-wrecked by DB combat builds. I bet if I ran a DB melee build vs a Tyrant Lizard I could end the fight with almost full motes and willpower. If you wanted to be super safe you could do it while dual-wielding. At that point a full excellency gives you 24 attack dice without a stunt or using Crossfire Flash, and you're clashing it's best attack with 13 dice, and each time you win a clash your excellency becomes cheaper and cheaper, all the way to 0m. Even if you lose that clash it's damage is only 12, minimum 3, and no way to boost it or key special effects off of it, which means your artifact armor will soak it all up and plink 2, maybe 3 initiative off of you. Then you go back to clash town.<br /> <br /> I think a DB archer might be in some trouble, but otherwise all the other combat styles have ways that let them 1v1 a Lizard. Melee is just the one that's nearly 100% effective. Also bonus points for unleashing a Harnessed Firestorm Assault at somewhere around 35 initiative to almost clear the entire health track in one single action. Then the turn after you can Burning Fury Wreath to take out the last one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-23-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T10:58:04-07:00","id":1307251,"title":"","content":"That isn't to say that Tyrant Lizards aren't scary to DB parties, they have some aspects that can make it a little tense, but it's really only tense because not everyone there will be a full combat monster. The Tyrant Lizard has almost no chance of hitting the super defense focused characters, but if your water aspect who has a mundane dagger, 2 awareness, 1 perception, 2 melee and 2 dex is in the fight, then he's looking prime for a good chomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:05:20-07:00","id":1307253,"title":"","content":"bureaucrats really shouldn't try hunting giant lizards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:07:09-07:00","id":1307254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307253#post1307253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bureaucrats really shouldn't try hunting giant lizards</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>shouldn't</i>, but for some reason in my games they so often do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:22:49-07:00","id":1307259,"title":"","content":"I just checked and the only Balanced Dodge charm is the Excellency. Flickering Candle Meditation and Ember-Amid-Smoke Misdirection are very much Fire element charms that boost defense and are not Balanced","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:36:16-07:00","id":1307262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307259#post1307259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just checked and the only Balanced Dodge charm is the Excellency. Flickering Candle Meditation and Ember-Amid-Smoke Misdirection are very much Fire element charms that boost defense and are not Balanced</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this directed at me? Because I did bring up both of those charms. Flickering Candle is good, but the excellency negates a point of environmental penalty all on its own, so it\u2019s best use is against things like onslaught or wound penalties. Not insignificant, but hardly a monopoly on Evasive charms.<br /> <br /> Ember-Amid-Smoke is a 3m charm that raises your evasion by +1, so in that way it\u2019s just worse than the excellency. Thankfully it also gives you a withering damage counter attack kind of thing, so it\u2019s worth the 3m, but it\u2019s not costing anyone Evasion by not having access to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T13:18:49-07:00","id":1307286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307259#post1307259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just checked and the only Balanced Dodge charm is the Excellency. Flickering Candle Meditation and Ember-Amid-Smoke Misdirection are very much Fire element charms that boost defense and are not Balanced</div> </div> </div> </div>Resistence suffers similar issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T22:32:03-07:00","id":1307418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307262#post1307262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was this directed at me? Because I did bring up both of those charms. Flickering Candle is good, but the excellency negates a point of environmental penalty all on its own, so it\u2019s best use is against things like onslaught or wound penalties. Not insignificant, but hardly a monopoly on Evasive charms.<br /> <br /> Ember-Amid-Smoke is a 3m charm that raises your evasion by +1, so in that way it\u2019s just worse than the excellency. Thankfully it also gives you a withering damage counter attack kind of thing, so it\u2019s worth the 3m, but it\u2019s not costing anyone Evasion by not having access to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the way you said it implied, at least to me, that there were several more Balanced dodge charms. It felt a bit weird to go and look and find out that, rather than there being a nice suite of Balanced defensive dodge charms with a couple of less useful ones being not Balanced, you were instead talking about the only three fire based defense boosting dodge charms and your argument basically boiled down to \u201cthe only useful fire based defense charm in Dodge is the Excellency.\u201d<br /> <br /> Which...feels different than what you were saying and makes taking DB Dodge at all sound like a trap.<br /> <br /> Especially since DB Melee has 4 Balanced Charms at its base and a defensive Water charm. Plus Elemental Sheath and Dragon Graced Weapon, which are both pan elemental. So if you\u2019re going to dip into something for defense, it sounds like Melee might be a better option than Dodge, especially if you want Water aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T09:15:22-07:00","id":1307495,"title":"","content":"Resistance is better for keeping a Water Aura than Dodge; arguably better than keeping an Earth Aura.<br /> <br /> Even the Signature Water Dodge Charm is about reducing the damage of an attack that hits you, which would seem to synergize well with soak-enhancing, damage-reducing Resistance Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T15:20:26-07:00","id":1307598,"title":"","content":"Dodge and Resistance more or less only being good for losing Aura and not gaining it definitely seems to be the main problem here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:00:42-07:00","id":1307604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307418#post1307418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the way you said it implied, at least to me, that there were several more Balanced dodge charms. It felt a bit weird to go and look and find out that, rather than there being a nice suite of Balanced defensive dodge charms with a couple of less useful ones being not Balanced, you were instead talking about the only three fire based defense boosting dodge charms and your argument basically boiled down to \u201cthe only useful fire based defense charm in Dodge is the Excellency.\u201d<br /> <br /> Which...feels different than what you were saying and makes taking DB Dodge at all sound like a trap.<br /> <br /> Especially since DB Melee has 4 Balanced Charms at its base and a defensive Water charm. Plus Elemental Sheath and Dragon Graced Weapon, which are both pan elemental. So if you\u2019re going to dip into something for defense, it sounds like Melee might be a better option than Dodge, especially if you want Water aura.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that depends on what you want to do with it. For one if you want to attack with melee then absolutely, that's barely even a question, use melee for defense. If you're not using melee though dodge has some advantages. For example if you're a bow-fighter you want to use Dodge because it lets you escape from a melee and get into your preferred range-band to attack with. Disengage is dodge based and Water Dodge especially uses it.<br /> <br /> You might also look at Heat of Battle Advance and say that's a dead charm because it will prevent you from getting into Water Aura, but if you're a Water Archer there are only 2 Archery charms in the tree that interact with Water Aura; the signature, which only uses aura for it's decisive attack secondary effect, and Arrow Rain Tempest, which is an Essence 5 decisive, so you should have plenty of opportunities where you don't care about your aura to use it. Thrown similarly has only one charm that interacts with Water Aura, and only on it's secondary effect.<br /> <br /> For that matter Flickering Candle and Hopping Firecracker aren't so bad either, Firecracker also helping you get to range, or even further. I also wouldn't grab Ember-Amid-Smoke or Bonfire Shadow Evasion, unless you're a fire aspect. Ember-Amid-Smoke maybe if you're trying to use out of aspect aura, but not Bonfire Shadow. Those might be considered traps.<br /> <br /> Brawl has a lot of charms that interact with Water Aura, it has 9, so that's a case where you might really feel the need to be sitting in Water Aura as much as possible, but Brawl is also a close ranged combat ability, that even has charms for reaching out and pulling people from range into close with you, so disengaging isn't such a big deal. If you're a Water Brawler you can take dodge anyway, but I wouldn't take more than the Excellency and the signature before Essence 5. At which point absolutely take up to Dragon-God-Dispersion, as described below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You might also want Dodge as someone like an Air or Wood Aspect for a lot of reasons. For one the Wood anima lets you ignore a point of penalty to your evasion, which stacks well with Dodge. If you're Air Elusive Crosswind Defense can let you sit at short/medium range from the melee, which means enemy archers are at medium/long range from you, and get cap-bursting defenses. Or just use Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, which is an incredibly powerful charm, and one that you can get just as you're able to pick up your second signature.<br /> <br /> Actually, I didn't really look at it much before but Dragon-God Dispersion is so damn good. Not only does it make Hopping Firecracker and Unassailable Body of Fire into whatever element you want, but some of the effects are great. If you're a wood archer it automatically grapples the thing you dodged from, letting you just sit back and fire arrows at while it's sat there unable to act, the Water one has a crippling -3 penalty for 3 whole turns, no way to spend willpower or anything to avoid it, and the Air one lets you move them a range band in any direction, which actually means that you can either push them away to get some space, OR drag them along with you if you want to pull them somewhere. All that is on top of an unblockable hardness ignoring decisive attack that builds onslaught penalty, and has the potential to deal further decisive damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also also \u201cthe only useful fire based defense charm in Dodge is the Excellency.\u201d is not exactly true. Bonfire shadow Evasion and Coiling Dragon Dance, especially when used together, are pretty solid, Coiling Dragon's duration of Aura makes it especially good. Double especially because there isn't a single Fire resistance charm that adds soak. If you're looking at that and going &quot;Wow, so my Wood aspect is screwed out of being able to protect herself then?&quot; then you missed the part where Wood basically gets Reed in the Wind as it's signature charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:06:29-07:00","id":1307605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307604#post1307604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Also also \u201cthe only useful fire based defense charm in Dodge is the Excellency.\u201d is not exactly true. Bonfire shadow Evasion and Coiling Dragon Dance, especially when used together, are pretty solid, Coiling Dragon's duration of Aura makes it especially good. Double especially because there isn't a single Fire resistance charm that adds soak. If you're looking at that and going &quot;Wow, so my Wood aspect is screwed out of being able to protect herself then?&quot; then you missed the part where Wood basically gets Reed in the Wind as it's signature charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those have aura and are fire based. They are useless to anyone not fire in any practical situation where you need a persistant scenelong aura.<br /> <br /> Also, a charm like reed in the wind is amazing. Swaying grass evasion is only good with other charms. +2 by itself can only take you so far. reed in the wind has other benefits and compunds with every other charm solars have. Dragon blooded only have a much weaker version that doesn't work with the rest of dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-24-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:08:51-07:00","id":1307606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307605#post1307605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those have aura and are fire based. They are useless to anyone not fire in any practical situation where you need a persistant scenelong aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, so they fill the quoted \u201cuseful fire based Defense charm, that isn\u2019t the excellency.\u201d There are useful fire based charms in dodge, but there are also some of the best charms in dodge that fire aura locks you out of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:21:18-07:00","id":1307609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307606#post1307606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct, so they fill the quoted \u201cuseful fire based Defense charm, that isn\u2019t the excellency.\u201d There are useful fire based charms in dodge, but there are also some of the best charms in dodge that fire aura locks you out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they didn't because they lock you out of grass swaying evasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:59:23-07:00","id":1307617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307609#post1307609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they didn't because they lock you out of grass swaying evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Flow With Strife, and Unmoving Centre of Enlightenment, and Elusive Crosswind Defense, and of you want to keep Fire Aura Virtuous Negation Defense and Ebbing Tide Recedes.<br /> <br /> Even with all that Fire probably has the best dodge, by a margin, but it also has the worst resistance. Because Fire in general has a really strong theme of being elusive and deadly, but fragile. That\u2019s why 3 different Fire dodge charms are about or include hurting people that fail to hit you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:03:43-07:00","id":1307618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307605#post1307605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a charm like reed in the wind is amazing. Swaying grass evasion is only good with other charms. +2 by itself can only take you so far. reed in the wind has other benefits and compunds with every other charm solars have. Dragon blooded only have a much weaker version that doesn't work with the rest of dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works with the only other charm that boost Defense, apart from Crosswind Defense, and Reed in the Wind has one other effect, which is a successful dodge gets you 1m back once per round. It\u2019s a SOLAR charm, the very best in the game.<br /> <br /> And if you want to talk about how much it sucks that DBs are so bad, go read my Arena thread, where they\u2019re so far undefeated and wrecking all comers, even 1v1 against a Tyrant Lizard and Nephwrack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:48:15-07:00","id":1307638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307617#post1307617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Flow With Strife, and Unmoving Centre of Enlightenment, and Elusive Crosswind Defense, and of you want to keep Fire Aura Virtuous Negation Defense and Ebbing Tide Recedes.<br /> <br /> Even with all that Fire probably has the best dodge, by a margin, but it also has the worst resistance. Because Fire in general has a really strong theme of being elusive and deadly, but fragile. That\u2019s why 3 different Fire dodge charms are about or include hurting people that fail to hit you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This is terrible design and I feel we should stop talking in circles. You clearly like it and I just see it as making the dragon blooded unfun. It's not fun to be permanently locked out of charms. It's not fun having to buy charms that you cannot use or you'll be hindered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T23:39:28-07:00","id":1307697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307638#post1307638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. This is terrible design and I feel we should stop talking in circles. You clearly like it and I just see it as making the dragon blooded unfun. It's not fun to be permanently locked out of charms. It's not fun having to buy charms that you cannot use or you'll be hindered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm sorry you don't like it but I think it's great, apart from a couple really dumb choices about where certain charms are placed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T07:09:48-07:00","id":1307746,"title":"","content":"I think Aura's great. The implementation isn't always best, but it's great how it forces/encourages Dragon-Blooded to work together so that each can perform at their best.<br /> <br /> I like how it encourages an Earth Aspect to use his Water-aspected Resistance Charms instead of the Earth ones, because he's already used the Water-aspected Brawl Charms he knows instead of the Earth-aspected ones in order to adapt to the weaknesses of his current opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T07:14:29-07:00","id":1307748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307746#post1307746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Aura's great. The implementation isn't always best, but it's great how it forces/encourages Dragon-Blooded to work together so that each can perform at their best.<br /> <br /> I like how it encourages an Earth Aspect to use his Water-aspected Resistance Charms instead of the Earth ones, because he's already used the Water-aspected Brawl Charms he knows instead of the Earth-aspected ones in order to adapt to the weaknesses of his current opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which stop working when he hits bonfire so he's limited in how he can use his charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T07:23:58-07:00","id":1307750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307748#post1307748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which stop working when he hits bonfire so he's limited in how he can use his charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he has the Earth-aspected ones to fall back upon, potentially including Firmament-Shattering Impact and Perfected Scales of the Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly 