f=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307751#post1307751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if he's used any aura long charms he's just wasted resources such as willpower he won't get back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resources exist to be spent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:33:26-07:00","id":1307799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307751#post1307751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if he's used any aura long charms he's just wasted resources such as willpower he won't get back.</div> </div> </div> </div>So he just doesn't use them, or even learn them, because he fucking KNOWS he's an Earth Aspect who will convert any Aura into an Earth Aura when he goes bonfire. He knows the risks and he takes his chances.<br /> <br /> The lack of higher-level Earth-aspected damage-reduction Charms is a problem, but it doesn't make Auras bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:49:14-07:00","id":1307801,"title":"","content":"I don't think Auras are bad per se, but I DO think that the &quot;lock into your own Aspect's Aura when you hit bonfire&quot; thing could go and it would solve SO MANY of the grievances with the current implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T11:28:50-07:00","id":1307808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307801#post1307801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Auras are bad per se, but I DO think that the &quot;lock into your own Aspect's Aura when you hit bonfire&quot; thing could go and it would solve SO MANY of the grievances with the current implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely open to discussion on THAT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T12:28:38-07:00","id":1307817,"title":"","content":"There <i>are</i> a few Charms that it\u2019s the only practical way to use but that\u2019s a problem with those Charms and one fixed by inventing literally one on-turn Charm of the right ability+element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T12:50:17-07:00","id":1307819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307817#post1307817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>are</i> a few Charms that it\u2019s the only practical way to use but that\u2019s a problem with those Charms and one fixed by inventing literally one on-turn Charm of the right ability+element.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best of both worlds is having the OPTION to convert any Aura you've got into the Aura of your Aspect when you hit bonfire, which means you don't get locked out of some of your Charms but you can also access other Charms you may not have any other possible way to access.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is the best solution, merely one that offers flexibility.<br /> <br /> I don't think Mela's Forking Tongue is as big a problem (if a problem at all), compared to Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T13:00:02-07:00","id":1307821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307819#post1307819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Mela's Forking Tongue is as big a problem (if a problem at all), compared to Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s funny, I actually think it\u2019s totally the other way around. Revolving Hurricane Force is reflexive and air aura, so just attack with an air charm on your turn and immediately after you can bag the aura for it. <br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019d be a lot happier changing it to your suggestion though than getting rid of it entirely. I would hate to lose the connection that it has with your aspect and turn the whole thing into a completely trivial mix and match. Aspect is supposed to be a really defining thing, I think 2e even said that DBs were possibly better described as 5 different kinds of exalt that were closely related. It might still be too easy for my tastes, but at least a wood aspect would be able to flare and automatically switch to wood aura and an Air couldn\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T13:10:16-07:00","id":1307823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307821#post1307821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s funny, I actually think it\u2019s totally the other way around. Revolving Hurricane Force is reflexive and air aura, so just attack with an air charm on your turn and immediately after you can bag the aura for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019d be a lot happier changing it to your suggestion though than getting rid of it entirely. I would hate to lose the connection that it has with your aspect and turn the whole thing into a completely trivial mix and match. Aspect is supposed to be a really defining thing, I think 2e even said that DBs were possibly better described as 5 different kinds of exalt that were closely related. It might still be too easy for my tastes, but at least a wood aspect would be able to flare and automatically switch to wood aura and an Air couldn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's much easier to put back up your persistant defese that costs 1 wp per activation over a move that you only use as a killing blow. I don't think you understand how different those are.<br /> <br /> Edit- Having reread the charm it's even worse. If you have the charm on and turn aura off you can't even reactivate it. So you basically just wasted a massive soak bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-25-2019, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T13:16:38-07:00","id":1307826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307821#post1307821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s funny, I actually think it\u2019s totally the other way around. Revolving Hurricane Force is reflexive and air aura, so just attack with an air charm on your turn and immediately after you can bag the aura for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>People who learn and rely on Air Charms don't tend to be people who invest so deeply into RESISTANCE, which is primarily Water and Earth until that one Air Charm.<br /> <br /> RHFD is an Air Charm that requires an Air Aura, sitting behind two Charms that require Water Aura, one Charm that requires Earth, Water, or Wood Aura, and one Charm at the very beginning which is Balanced to let you keep an Aura Aura. The best way to get a Water Aura is to invest in Brawl, which benefits from Resistance Charms which benefit from Brawl's Water Aura. To a lesser degree, the same is true of Earth and Wood Auras.<br /> <br /> But Mela's Forking Tongue is something that your Lore-specialist friend gives you their Air Aura in order to get the most out of the Charm, like Lucca throwing fire onto Chrono's blade for a Dual Tech. Or else it's an Air Aspect's reward for investing so deep into all of those Fire Melee Charms which are conspicuously, with no third element sitting between the Fire Charms and that one Air Charm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T14:42:48-07:00","id":1307853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307819#post1307819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best of both worlds is having the OPTION to convert any Aura you've got into the Aura of your Aspect when you hit bonfire, which means you don't get locked out of some of your Charms but you can also access other Charms you may not have any other possible way to access.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is the best solution, merely one that offers flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>An alternative I thought of a while back would be changing &quot;If you would enter an off-Aspect Aura while at bonfire you don't enter Aura at all&quot; to &quot;If you would enter an off-Aspect Aura while at bonfire you enter your Aspect Aura instead.&quot; For most Abilities though I'm pretty sure that would be even stronger than ditching bonfire-affects-Aura entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T15:39:05-07:00","id":1307865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307823#post1307823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it's much easier to put back up your persistant defese that costs 1 wp per activation over a move that you only use as a killing blow. I don't think you understand how different those are.<br /> <br /> Edit- Having reread the charm it's even worse. If you have the charm on and turn aura off you can't even reactivate it. So you basically just wasted a massive soak bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, yeah, don't leave Air Aura once you've activated the charm. You've seen how good it is combined with the Air signature right? Lets say that you're not even wearing heavy armor, just light, because you're an air aspect and you're using dodge as your primary defense, that's cool. You're still going for big soak with your resistance charms, so you've got 5 stamina, that's a base soak of 10. Decent, but nothing super special. Then you activate Revolving Hurricane Force Defense, and lets also say you don't have an applicable specialty, they don't always happen, but you get 5 free non-charm dice, and can still 5m excellency it for 20 dice, that's about 10 more soak.<br /> <br /> So now you're sitting at 20 soak, but what if you activate it AND the signature at the same time? Body Like Clouds Meditation reduces the damage roll by Essence, so in this case 5, minimum 1 even below minimum damage. So now if you take a 26 damage attack, with an Overwhelming 6 Grand Daiklave, you soak that down to a single die of damage. At which point there's a 60% chance that it doesn't roll any damage and they lose 2 initiative, which you then gain.<br /> <br /> Then on top of that, Impervious Skin of Stone is balanced, which means if you're worried that you might take more than a 26 damage attack, which is damn big, even for other Exalted to reach, you can use ISoS to soak everything up to 31 damage. That's <i>stupid </i>good. If you're in a group you will now never be the target of withering attacks because it's totally pointless, and if you're in a 1v1 duel you just sit back and laugh because they can't do anything.<br /> <br /> The best they could do is, if they aren't crashed, launch one last decisive attack against you and hope it does something. If they can't, game over. All that's going to happen is they attack you, 60% chance of losing 2i, 30% chance of doing 1 damage, 10% chance of doing 2 damage. Then you wither them back and it just keeps going until you've got as much initiative as you please, and then decisive them. They'll slowly chip away at the shield, sure, but how many free attacks do you need to win? Especially when more than half the time they're giving you initiative by withering you.<br /> <br /> If you could have that combo and be an Earth aspect at bonfire you'd just get another free 5 soak out of that<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh yeah, and if you're wearing heavy artifact plate instead of light armour, increase all those values by 6<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307826#post1307826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who learn and rely on Air Charms don't tend to be people who invest so deeply into RESISTANCE, which is primarily Water and Earth until that one Air Charm.<br /> <br /> RHFD is an Air Charm that requires an Air Aura, sitting behind two Charms that require Water Aura, one Charm that requires Earth, Water, or Wood Aura, and one Charm at the very beginning which is Balanced to let you keep an Aura Aura. The best way to get a Water Aura is to invest in Brawl, which benefits from Resistance Charms which benefit from Brawl's Water Aura. To a lesser degree, the same is true of Earth and Wood Auras.<br /> <br /> But Mela's Forking Tongue is something that your Lore-specialist friend gives you their Air Aura in order to get the most out of the Charm, like Lucca throwing fire onto Chrono's blade for a Dual Tech. Or else it's an Air Aspect's reward for investing so deep into all of those Fire Melee Charms which are conspicuously, with no third element sitting between the Fire Charms and that one Air Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh the placement, yeah I've said on this thread before that I think the placement is really stupid. It should either come off the air sig or at least just Earth Bears Witness or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T15:49:53-07:00","id":1307868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307865#post1307865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, yeah, don't leave Air Aura once you've activated the charm. You've seen how good it is combined with the Air signature right? Lets say that you're not even wearing heavy armor, just light, because you're an air aspect and you're using dodge as your primary defense, that's cool. You're still going for big soak with your resistance charms, so you've got 5 stamina, that's a base soak of 10. Decent, but nothing super special. Then you activate Revolving Hurricane Force Defense, and lets also say you don't have an applicable specialty, they don't always happen, but you get 5 free non-charm dice, and can still 5m excellency it for 20 dice, that's about 10 more soak.<br /> <br /> So now you're sitting at 20 soak, but what if you activate it AND the signature at the same time? Body Like Clouds Meditation reduces the damage roll by Essence, so in this case 5, minimum 1 even below minimum damage. So now if you take a 26 damage attack, with an Overwhelming 6 Grand Daiklave, you soak that down to a single die of damage. At which point there's a 60% chance that it doesn't roll any damage and they lose 2 initiative, which you then gain.<br /> <br /> Then on top of that, Impervious Skin of Stone is balanced, which means if you're worried that you might take more than a 26 damage attack, which is damn big, even for other Exalted to reach, you can use ISoS to soak everything up to 31 damage. That's <i>stupid </i>good. If you're in a group you will now never be the target of withering attacks because it's totally pointless, and if you're in a 1v1 duel you just sit back and laugh because they can't do anything.<br /> <br /> The best they could do is, if they aren't crashed, launch one last decisive attack against you and hope it does something. If they can't, game over. All that's going to happen is they attack you, 60% chance of losing 2i, 30% chance of doing 1 damage, 10% chance of doing 2 damage. Then you wither them back and it just keeps going until you've got as much initiative as you please, and then decisive them. They'll slowly chip away at the shield, sure, but how many free attacks do you need to win? Especially when more than half the time they're giving you initiative by withering you.<br /> <br /> If you could have that combo and be an Earth aspect at bonfire you'd just get another free 5 soak out of that<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh yeah, and if you're wearing heavy artifact plate instead of light armour, increase all those values by 6</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet you have to buy several charms you can't use at all and if for any reason you are kicked out of the aura or have to expend it and fail you are screwed. Also, flurries will bring it down quickly and that's assuming you roll the average. It also does nothing against decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> I would like to reiterate that I don't have a problem with dragon blooded being weaker. Their charms even if they had access to their entire tree still don't feel like they'd be remotely on the level of a celestial because the effects are already quite weaker than what solars or lunars get. My issues stem from the fact that you can't use every charm you have to buy and you are punished for attempting to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-25-2019, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:01:34-07:00","id":1307881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307868#post1307868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you have to buy several charms you can't use at all and if for any reason you are kicked out of the aura or have to expend it and fail you are screwed. Also, flurries will bring it down quickly and that's assuming you roll the average.</div> </div> </div> </div>...why are you still bringing up that it's in a crappy place in the tree when I've said three times now that I also think that...?<br /> <br /> Also, you could roll less, maybe, you could roll more too. You could even stunt and/or spend willpower if you wanted. A two die stunt is pretty easy, so actually the average is more like 6 since who isn't going to stunt that? It's cool as hell, which makes for easy stunts. A Grand Daiklave wielded by somebody with 5 Strength has a base damage of 19. so if you roll 4, say, solidly below average, they still need to somehow boost their damage by more than 6 to roll just 2 damage. That is the best case damage scenario, and they're using a crappy low-accuracy weapon to do it, so it's not because they beat your defense by 6. Even then...great? You're now rolling 2 damage for whatever crazy charm investment you had to put up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Flurries aren't even bad either. Because you have a 60% chance to steal 2i, a 30% chance to lose 1, and a 10% chance to lose 2, you actually come out of flurries on top. Lunar uses Thousand Claw Affliction? Bring it on, that's 5 withering attacks that will give me more initiative than they drain, and cost 4m, 4i, 1wp to trigger. Solars don't even have a withering flurry.<br /> <br /> Decisive flurries are almost as bad, the only reason they're not worse is that they're not actively detrimental. You want to activate Iron Whirlwind Attack with 10 initiative? Awesome! How are you ignoring my hardness again? Ah, that's right, you aren't, because Solar melee HAS no Supplemental charms that ignore hardness, only Simple ones that can't be combined with flurries. Even the mighty Thunderbolt Attack Prana is useless here, since it doesn't affect damage dice before they're rolled. Also, they're decisive, so I hope you're willing to spend some motes to hit reliably, or those first couple attacks stand a decent chance of missing because that's how probability distributions work. Even if they do all hit, because you didn't get past my hardness you spend like 10m and a willpower to reduce the withering shield of a Dragonblooded by 5 points. For a Solar, that's pathetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless you mean if you're facing a Dawn Caste Solar with a bunch of initiative, Invincible Fury of the Dawn, motes, decisive damage enhancing charms, and excellency dice that he's willing to spend to hit you. In which case congratulations, omae wa mou shindeiru, you are already dead. There is nothing in the game that can survive that short of another celestial exalt who is very focused on defense. You can't even flurry-break out of it with Leaping Dodge Method because Invincible Fury of the Dawn lets you jump a range band with every attack. Think that's shitty? I do too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Against anything other than that, the charm combo is unbelievably good. So in 98% of fights.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, maybe, maybe, a DB in Earth Aura using Perfected Scales of the Dragon with Essence 5 could survive that kind of assault, but since the Solar wouldn't miss with all the attacks the DB would have to keep using Perfected Scales of the Dragon each turn afterwards and doing nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-25-2019, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:03:34-07:00","id":1307883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307868#post1307868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to reiterate that I don't have a problem with dragon blooded being weaker. Their charms even if they had access to their entire tree still don't feel like they'd be remotely on the level of a celestial because the effects are already quite weaker than what solars or lunars get. My issues stem from the fact that you can't use every charm you have to buy and you are punished for attempting to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, there should not be in any way a line of Water Aura charms that lead up to an Air Aura charm, especially not when it has Duration: Aura, which means you want to sit in it once you get it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:06:51-07:00","id":1307885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307881#post1307881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Against anything other than that, the charm combo is unbelievably good. So in 98% of fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it also lose out to getting dog piled? Like it's a fine combo. But I don't think having to wait till E5 and taking several dead charms you can't use is a fair trade off. Other exalts beyond DBs even at their level aren't going to have to deal with such a shitty limiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:11:45-07:00","id":1307887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307883#post1307883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this, there should not be in any way a line of Water Aura charms that lead up to an Air Aura charm, especially not when it has Duration: Aura, which means you want to sit in it once you get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say another issue I have with aura. Is Duration: Aura. It should honestly just be scenelong but stop working on turns when your aura isn't up. Losing a charm because you had to expend aura just doesn't make you want to waste it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:16:27-07:00","id":1307889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307885#post1307885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't it also lose out to getting dog piled? Like it's a fine combo. But I don't think having to wait till E5 and taking several dead charms you can't use is a fair trade off. Other exalts beyond DBs even at their level aren't going to have to deal with such a shitty limiter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if you're getting dogpiled it's amazing. The worst things, by far, about being dogpiled are the onslaught penalties, and the minimum damage ticks. If four people are beating on you with regular old daiklaves, and hitting, they're dealing 20 minimum damage every turn. With this combo up they're dealing 4, and when they fail to roll damage feeding you initiative. Maybe they pound through your shield in 2 rounds because of it, but during those 2 rounds you would have taken 40 withering damage, and took 8 instead, and got bonus initiative for it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course that's assuming you're facing off against 4 people who can wield daiklaves. That's really bad news. Best case scenario they're DBs, and I've been running combat after combat after combat of 1 Lunar vs 3 DBs and the Lunars haven't won one yet. They haven't even killed one of the DBs in the process of losing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-25-2019, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:20:40-07:00","id":1307891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307889#post1307889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually if you're getting dogpiled it's amazing. The worst things, by far, about being dogpiled are the onslaught penalties, and the minimum damage ticks. If four people are beating on you with regular old daiklaves, and hitting, they're dealing 20 minimum damage every turn. With this combo up they're dealing 4, and when they fail to roll damage feeding you initiative. Maybe they pound through your shield in 2 rounds because of it, but during those 2 rounds you would have taken 40 withering damage, and took 8 instead, and got bonus initiative for it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course that's assuming you're facing off against 4 people who can wield daiklaves. That's really bad news. Best case scenario they're DBs, and I've been running combat after combat after combat of 1 Lunar vs 3 DBs and the Lunars haven't won one yet. They haven't even killed one of the DBs in the process of losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't those E1 lunars? I mean E3 is when they really get their more dangerous charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:25:25-07:00","id":1307893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307891#post1307891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't those E1 lunars? I mean E3 is when they really get their more dangerous charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly E2, but some of us were doing some theorycrafting for e3 and maybe like one or two really specific builds has much of a chance, if they get lucky. Otherwise they just run mote dry trying to defend themselves and attack at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:27:09-07:00","id":1307896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307893#post1307893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly E2, but some of us were doing some theorycrafting for e3 and maybe like one or two really specific builds has much of a chance, if they get lucky. Otherwise they just run mote dry trying to defend themselves and attack at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't completely read lunars but they don't have the same scenelong onslaught charms?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:28:31-07:00","id":1307897,"title":"","content":"These are Essence 3 DBs mind you, so they have signature charms. On the other hand they\u2019re also not E5.<br /> <br /> I think an essence 4-5 Lunar could maybe take them though. But it wouldn\u2019t be 100%.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I wouldn\u2019t really want to be a DB fighting an E3 Lunar either just because I might die. We probably won\u2019t lose the fight but I might die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:30:54-07:00","id":1307898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307896#post1307896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't completely read lunars but they don't have the same scenelong onslaught charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at essence two even. It doesn\u2019t matter the dragon blood it full Excellency every attack you can not rely solely on your base defence when an artefact weapon is coming for you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:55:40-07:00","id":1307904,"title":"","content":"I mean, as of right now there's no actual way to force a dragon blooded out of their Aura. The scene can end or you can go Bonfire but you can avoid going Bonfire, especially if you're refilling your Personal pool with your combat and stunt motes.<br /> You can't get &quot;Kicked out&quot; by any effect that is currently published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T18:24:52-07:00","id":1307909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307904#post1307904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, as of right now there's no actual way to force a dragon blooded out of their Aura. The scene can end or you can go Bonfire but you can avoid going Bonfire, especially if you're refilling your Personal pool with your combat and stunt motes.<br /> You can't get &quot;Kicked out&quot; by any effect that is currently published.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motes do not refill with stunts in Third Edition. Stunts only give you dice, successes, and Willpower in return. +2 dice, +2 dice +1 sux +1 WP, or +2 dice +2 sux +2 WP, respectively. There is basically no way, except holding back and doing even more poorly than usual, to not enter bonfire anima by your second or third round, particularly if you need to juggle attack and defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:05:38-07:00","id":1307934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307909#post1307909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Motes do not refill with stunts in Third Edition. Stunts only give you dice, successes, and Willpower in return. +2 dice, +2 dice +1 sux +1 WP, or +2 dice +2 sux +2 WP, respectively. There is basically no way, except holding back and doing even more poorly than usual, to not enter bonfire anima by your second or third round, particularly if you need to juggle attack and defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Anima only jumps if you spend 5 peripheral at once.<br /> <br /> Need to spend 5m in an instant? Spend 4 peripheral and 1 personal. Always spend 4m out of your peripheral pool before touching personal and you can really avoid anima flare. If you're spending more than 5m a turn you're gonna flare and get mote tapped eventually but you can push it off a good long while with careful management.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:19:22-07:00","id":1307938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307934#post1307934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that Anima only jumps if you spend 5 peripheral at once.<br /> <br /> Need to spend 5m in an instant? Spend 4 peripheral and 1 personal. Always spend 4m out of your peripheral pool before touching personal and you can really avoid anima flare. If you're spending more than 5m a turn you're gonna flare and get mote tapped eventually but you can push it off a good long while with careful management.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can't spend 4m from Peripheral and 1m from Personal unless you're spending 4m for one thing and 1m for a different thing. If your Charm costs 5m+, you can't divide the costs. A lot of DB Charms cost 5m+. It's not as easy as you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:38:19-07:00","id":1307940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307934#post1307934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that Anima only jumps if you spend 5 peripheral at once.<br /> <br /> Need to spend 5m in an instant? Spend 4 peripheral and 1 personal. Always spend 4m out of your peripheral pool before touching personal and you can really avoid anima flare. If you're spending more than 5m a turn you're gonna flare and get mote tapped eventually but you can push it off a good long while with careful management.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, that's not possible. Motes must be spent from entirely one pool or the other, unless they empty one of the pools. So doing the double dip is only possible if you're riding the line and emptying personal every time.<br /> <br /> Not flaring isn't generally so hard though. Dragonblooded can only spend 4m on an excellency unless they have 5 in the ability and an applicable specialty, which isn't really all the time. Also you regen 5 motes a round, so if you start spending out of your personal you're only getting closer to your peripheral by (motes spent -5).<br /> <br /> Double also, you only jump up 2 levels at once when you spend 10+ peripheral motes, so you can spend 9 two actions in a row and not go bonfire.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it is restrictive. If you pick aura charms that have an aura outside your aspect, there will be times when you will want to spend more motes than that, but can't. I wouldn't necessarily suggest going full hog because of that. Like if you're a fire aspect who wants to brawl, take things like Hammering Wave and Oaken Thew Exertion. You can then combine them for a +10 to damage, or enter Water Aura if you want for the benefit of keeping onslaught penalties up. For your signature consider taking Erupting Fury Barrage instead of Embracing the Violent Flow, though. Basically if you're an Air Aspect, why are none of your offensive or defensive charms Air?<br /> <br /> The other thing is that Dragonblooded have really kickass anima powers, and anima flux. An Essence 2 Wood Aspect with 5 Stamina exposes all with a 7 round duration, 2i/round poison, which is more difficult to resist than Arrow Frog Venom.<br /> <br /> But then again your anima destroys the environment, so if you're somewhere you don't want trashed by a firestorm for fifteen minutes. So there's other strong benefits to keeping it in check as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:50:15-07:00","id":1307943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307940#post1307940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, that's not possible. Motes must be spent from entirely one pool or the other, unless they empty one of the pools. So doing the double dip is only possible if you're riding the line and emptying personal every time.<br /> <br /> Not flaring isn't generally so hard though. Dragonblooded can only spend 4m on an excellency unless they have 5 in the ability and an applicable specialty, which isn't really all the time. Also you regen 5 motes a round, so if you start spending out of your personal you're only getting closer to your peripheral by (motes spent -5).<br /> <br /> Double also, you only jump up 2 levels at once when you spend 10+ peripheral motes, so you can spend 9 two actions in a row and not go bonfire.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it is restrictive. If you pick aura charms that have an aura outside your aspect, there will be times when you will want to spend more motes than that, but can't. I wouldn't necessarily suggest going full hog because of that. Like if you're a fire aspect who wants to brawl, take things like Hammering Wave and Oaken Thew Exertion. You can then combine them for a +10 to damage, or enter Water Aura if you want for the benefit of keeping onslaught penalties up. For your signature consider taking Erupting Fury Barrage instead of Embracing the Violent Flow, though. Basically if you're an Air Aspect, why are none of your offensive or defensive charms Air?<br /> <br /> The other thing is that Dragonblooded have really kickass anima powers, and anima flux. An Essence 2 Wood Aspect with 5 Stamina exposes all with a 7 round duration, 2i/round poison, which is more difficult to resist than Arrow Frog Venom.<br /> <br /> But then again your anima destroys the environment, so if you're somewhere you don't want trashed by a firestorm for fifteen minutes. So there's other strong benefits to keeping it in check as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Bit of a correction, you CAN spend motes from different pools as long as they are separate things. For example, you can use a 4m Melee Excellency from Peripheral motes while also using Burning Fury Wreath from Personal, but you can't use Burning Fury Wreath by paying some Personal motes and some Peripheral motes unless doing so empties one of the pools and you still have motes to carry over. Also, DBs can only spend 4m on an excellency unless they have 5 in the Ability OR 4 and a specialty OR both. Their Excellencies go up to 6m with Ability 5 + Specialty. Between offensive and defensive Charms or even just Excellencies, the 5m regen barely matters since you're spending so much more than that. You can spend 9 motes in a single action and you go from Dim to Burning, then just spending 5m more makes you go Bonfire, the amount keeps being 5m to go a step up.<br /> <br /> Anima flux doesn't matter in most fights where it should, because it turns off when 1) Your opponent is another Dragon-Blood, or 2) Your opponent has Hardness. In most actually important fights, one of the two will be true, be it because they're tough animals, DB rivals, Exalts or spirits with Artifact Armor, or the same Exalts or Spirits with Hardness-granting Charms. And yet it still destroys the environment, hurts your mount and mortal allies, and is in general more of a nuisance than a help most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:11:03-07:00","id":1307952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307943#post1307943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of a correction, you CAN spend motes from different pools as long as they are separate things. For example, you can use a 4m Melee Excellency from Peripheral motes while also using Burning Fury Wreath from Personal, but you can't use Burning Fury Wreath by paying some Personal motes and some Peripheral motes unless doing so empties one of the pools and you still have motes to carry over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Is that true? Like in one single attack, you can pay for 2 different charms out of 2 different pools?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307943#post1307943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, DBs can only spend 4m on an excellency unless they have 5 in the Ability OR 4 and a specialty OR both. Their Excellencies go up to 6m with Ability 5 + Specialty. Between offensive and defensive Charms or even just Excellencies, the 5m regen barely matters since you're spending so much more than that. You can spend 9 motes in a single action and you go from Dim to Burning, then just spending 5m more makes you go Bonfire, the amount keeps being 5m to go a step up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah right, thanks for that, for some reason I was stuck thinking about the charms that add successes instead of dice. That's true you just need Ability 5 to make that cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307943#post1307943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anima flux doesn't matter in most fights where it should, because it turns off when 1) Your opponent is another Dragon-Blood, or 2) Your opponent has Hardness. In most actually important fights, one of the two will be true, be it because they're tough animals, DB rivals, Exalts or spirits with Artifact Armor, or the same Exalts or Spirits with Hardness-granting Charms. And yet it still destroys the environment, hurts your mount and mortal allies, and is in general more of a nuisance than a help most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This though I debate. A crashed opponent has Hardness set to 0, also a crashed opponent is taking lethal instead of withering damage. If you manage to crash a non-dragonblooded exalt or powerful spirit they'll then be vulnerable to your anima, and taking health level damage to boot.<br /> <br /> You are absolutely right about mortal allies and mounts getting in the way though. I'm not even 100% sure how the mounts thing interacts, I guess just as a trivial foe, so they're always just taking straight lethal. I guess getting a bear or claw strider or something as a mount is just a lot more appealing before Essence 3. Perhaps there will be an artifact or something in the Realm book like there was in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:17:52-07:00","id":1307955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307952#post1307952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? Is that true? Like in one single attack, you can pay for 2 different charms out of 2 different pools?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah right, thanks for that, for some reason I was stuck thinking about the charms that add successes instead of dice. That's true you just need Ability 5 to make that cap.<br /> <br /> <br /> This though I debate. A crashed opponent has Hardness set to 0, also a crashed opponent is taking lethal instead of withering damage. If you manage to crash a non-dragonblooded exalt or powerful spirit they'll then be vulnerable to your anima, and taking health level damage to boot.<br /> <br /> You are absolutely right about mortal allies and mounts getting in the way though. I'm not even 100% sure how the mounts thing interacts, I guess just as a trivial foe, so they're always just taking straight lethal. I guess getting a bear or claw strider or something as a mount is just a lot more appealing before Essence 3. Perhaps there will be an artifact or something in the Realm book like there was in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, this is true. As long as they are different, you can split the costs. <br /> <br /> No problem<br /> <br /> Mounts get damaged by it narratively if they're not important combatants; expect them to get very hurt or even die if a DB spends too much time riding them while at Bonfire. Artifact Barding is already a thing that exists in Arms of the Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:22:52-07:00","id":1307956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307955#post1307955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is true. As long as they are different, you can split the costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mind is blown.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307955#post1307955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mounts get damaged by it narratively if they're not important combatants; expect them to get very hurt or even die if a DB spends too much time riding them while at Bonfire. Artifact Barding is already a thing that exists in Arms of the Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also looking at just regular barding and it suggests that it subtract raw decisive damage from incoming decisive attacks. Could regular barding protect from anima flux? Is there a ruling on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:25:11-07:00","id":1307957,"title":"","content":"I didn't even know that but I assume regular one doesn't cut it. It would be INSULTING if an enemy's mount could just ignore a burning demigod's fiery wreath because it got tailored with leather barding lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:28:07-07:00","id":1307958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307957#post1307957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't even know that but I assume regular one doesn't cut it. It would be INSULTING if an enemy's mount could just ignore a burning demigod's fiery wreath because it got tailored with leather barding lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually more than you think, heavy barding subtracts a straight 6 from the raw damage. That's massive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:29:16-07:00","id":1307959,"title":"","content":"Like I said. Would be downright insulting, regardless of how much normal damage it negates. I'd rule it out of my games. Artifact or bust.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, I also rule out the &quot;DB opponents aren't affected by it&quot;, make it not work on your own mount, and in general try to make it actually fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:39:56-07:00","id":1307964,"title":"","content":"The ruling from devs on the thread is that if the mount isn't important enough to roll into Initaitive, it's not important enough to track its wounds every turn via anima, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:42:52-07:00","id":1307966,"title":"","content":"The ruling is to not track it every turn BUT to track the damage narratively outside combat and even kill it if it's exposed for too long, which I ignore for the PC's own mount's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:42:52-07:00","id":1307967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307959#post1307959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said. Would be downright insulting, regardless of how much normal damage it negates. I'd rule it out of my games. Artifact or bust.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, I also rule out the &quot;DB opponents aren't affected by it&quot;, make it not work on your own mount, and in general try to make it actually fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just surprised more people aren't using barding, I've never heard anyone speak of it before. It's a great way to keep them alive in battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:43:42-07:00","id":1307968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1306125-the-aura-mechanic?p=1307967#post1307967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just surprised more people aren't using barding, I've never heard anyone speak of it before. It's a great way to keep them alive in battle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> People forget it's a thing, the same way they forget about, say, the insanity that Impaling Attacks are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}